//! Regular expressions that match in time linear in the subject: RE2's syntax, without
//! backreferences or lookaround, over a `String` a character at a time and over `Bytes` a byte at a
//! time.
//!
//! A pattern is compiled once, by `compile` to a `Result` or by `read`, which raises `regex.fail`.
//! An error reports why, and at which character of the pattern. `compile_bytes` and `read_bytes`
//! make a `ByteRegex`, whose pattern's characters are bytes. A pattern written in source is a
//! literal, `re"a+b"`, compiled when the program is checked (`std.re`).
//!
//! What a search costs. No search goes back over its subject to try another way: it follows every
//! state the pattern could be in at once, entering each at most once per position, so its steps
//! grow at most as the subject's length times the pattern's size, and for no pattern do they double
//! with one more character. When a subject is longer than `Options.short`, `is_match`, `find` and
//! `find_all` instead follow a single set of states at a time. They cache each set of states they
//! reach, together with the set that follows it for each byte, so each byte costs one table lookup.
//! They cache at most `Options.state_limit` sets; after that the search goes back to following
//! every state at once. A search skips straight to the next byte a match can start with, or to the
//! next occurrence of the text every match starts with. When every match contains some text, as
//! every match of `\w+@example\.com` contains `@example.com`, a subject without that text is ruled
//! out without being scanned, and a pattern that is plain text is found as text. Groups are
//! computed only when requested, and then only over the match. A pattern compiles to at most
//! `Options.size_limit` instructions, with each counted repetition written out, and a pattern past
//! that is rejected before it is built.
//!
//! The syntax is RE2's:
//!
//! - A character matches itself; `.` matches any character but a line feed; `\` before punctuation
//! is that character; `\a \f \n \r \t \v`, `\0` and up to two more octal digits, `\xNN` and
//! `\x{N...}` write one by its number; `\Q...\E` is its text taken literally. - `[abc]`, `[a-z]`
//! and `[^a-z]` are one character of a class. A `]` first in a class and a `-` first or last are
//! themselves. `\d`, `\w` and `\s` are a digit, a word character and white space; `\D`, `\W` and
//! `\S` every other character; and `[[:alpha:]]` and `[[:^alpha:]]` the POSIX classes; all of them
//! work inside or outside a class. - `\pL` and `\p{Greek}` are a character with a Unicode property,
//! and `\PL`, `\P{Greek}` and `\p{^Greek}` one without it, inside or outside a class, over text
//! only: a general category by its abbreviation or its name (`Lu`, `Uppercase_Letter`), a major
//! class (`L`, `Letter`), `LC`, a script by its name in the database (`Greek`, `Old_Italic`),
//! `Alphabetic`, `Lowercase`, `Uppercase`, `White_Space`, `XID_Start`, `XID_Continue`, and `Any`. -
//! `^` and `$` are the subject's start and its very end, never the position before a last line
//! feed, and `\A` and `\z` are those whatever the flags; `\b` is a word's edge and `\B` any other
//! position. - `xy` is `x` then `y`, and `x|y` either, with `x` preferred. - `x*`, `x+`, `x?`,
//! `x{n}`, `x{n,}` and `x{n,m}` repeat `x`, taking as much as they can, and with a `?` after, as
//! little as they can. A count is at most 1000, and a `{` that does not start a count matches
//! itself. - `(x)` is a group, numbered from 1 in the order of its `(`, `(?P<name>x)` or
//! `(?<name>x)` a group with a name, and `(?:x)` no group at all. - `(?i)` ignores case, `(?m)`
//! makes `^` and `$` a line's start and end, `(?s)` lets `.` match a line feed, `(?U)` swaps which
//! repetitions take as little as they can, and `(?u)` makes `\d`, `\w`, `\s` and `\b` Unicode's.
//! Each lasts to the end of the group it is written in; `(?i:x)` applies to `x` alone, and `(?-i)`
//! ends one.
//!
//! What is rejected, each with its own reason: a backreference (`\1`, `\k<name>`, `(?P=name)`) and
//! lookahead or lookbehind, either of which would cost more than linear steps; a repetition of a
//! repetition, such as a possessive `a*+`; `\C`; and a `\p` that names no property this module
//! reads. An octal escape starts with `\0`, so that `\1` to `\9` are always the backreferences they
//! are elsewhere.
//!
//! Unicode. A character is a code point. `.`, a class written out and a negated class all cover
//! every code point, and a match never ends inside one. `\d`, `\w`, `\s`, `\b` and the POSIX
//! classes are ASCII-only unless `(?u)` is written, as in RE2: a pattern is most often over a
//! protocol's text, where a digit is one of ten and a word's edge must not change with the Unicode
//! version. Under `(?u)`, `\d` is `\p{Nd}`, `\s` is `\p{White_Space}`, `\w` is UTS #18's word
//! character (alphabetic, a mark, a decimal digit, connector punctuation or a joiner), and `\b` is
//! an edge of a run of those. A search for a pattern with such a `\b` always follows every state at
//! once. `(?i)` folds case as Unicode's simple case folding does, so `(?i)k` also matches the
//! Kelvin sign, `(?i)σ` every sigma, and an accented letter its other case. A character whose other
//! case is several characters, such as `ß` and `SS`, is not paired with them. A pattern over bytes
//! folds only ASCII letters, and accepts no `\p` and no `(?u)`. The tables are from the Unicode
//! version that `std.ucd` names.
//!
//! Which match. Among the matches that start leftmost, a search returns the one that a backtracking
//! search would find first: that search tries alternatives in order, and tries each repetition's
//! longer option before its shorter. Perl and RE2 choose this way. `Options.longest` requests the
//! longest match at the leftmost start instead, as POSIX specifies; each group then matches the
//! text it would match in the first such longest match a backtracking search would find.
//! `find_all`, `captures_all`, `replace_all` and `split` take matches in order, none overlapping: a
//! search starts where the last match ended, or one character after an empty one, and an empty
//! match is skipped where the previous match ended.
//!
//! A `Span` counts characters of a `String` and bytes of a `Bytes`, as `String::slice` and
//! `Bytes::slice` do.
//!
//! When to use something else. A pattern over paths, with `**` and braces, belongs to `std.glob`.
//! Anything that nests, such as brackets that must balance or a grammar with a recursive rule, is
//! beyond what a regular expression can express. Text whose parts a program wants as values rather
//! than spans needs a parser: `std.parse` builds one from smaller ones.

import std.bytes (hex_value, is_digit, is_letter)
import std.char
import std.char (CodePointRange)
import std.laws (agrees)
import std.list (enumerate)
import std.math (ilog2)
import std.show (show)
import std.string
import std.ucd
import std.gen

/// Why a pattern, or a replacement template, is rejected.
pub type ErrorKind =
  /// A `(` with no `)`.
  | UnclosedGroup
  /// A `)` with no `(`.
  | UnopenedGroup
  /// A `[` that opens a class, where the pattern ends before the class is closed with `]`.
  | UnclosedClass
  /// A range in a class whose ends are out of order.
  | BadRange
  /// A `[:name:]` that is not a known class.
  | BadClassName
  /// A `\` with no character after it.
  | TrailingEscape
  /// A `\` before a letter or a digit that is not an escape here.
  | BadEscape
  /// A `*`, `+`, `?` or `{n,m}` with nothing before it to repeat.
  | NothingToRepeat
  /// A repetition of a repetition, such as `a**` and the possessive `a*+`.
  | NestedRepeat
  /// A count past 1000, or a `{n,m}` whose `n` is the greater.
  | BadRepeat
  /// A `(?` that starts nothing this dialect supports.
  | BadGroup
  /// A group's name that is empty or contains anything but letters, digits and `_`.
  | BadGroupName
  /// A name given to two groups.
  | DuplicateName
  /// `\1`, `\k<name>` or `(?P=name)`.
  | Backreference
  /// `(?=`, `(?!`, `(?<=` or `(?<!`.
  | Lookaround
  /// A `\p` or `\P` that names no property this module supports, or one in a pattern over bytes.
  | UnicodeProperty
  /// `\C` in a pattern over text.
  | HalfCharacter
  /// A character past `U+00FF` in a pattern over bytes.
  | NotAByte
  /// A pattern whose program would have more instructions than its limit.
  | TooLarge
  /// Groups nested more than 200 deep.
  | TooDeep
  /// A `$` in a template that is not followed by a group's number or name, or by a second `$`.
  | LoneDollar
  /// A `${` in a template with no `}`.
  | UnclosedName
  /// A template that names a group its pattern lacks.
  | NoSuchGroup

/// A compile error, and the offset of the character of the pattern or template it is about.
pub type Error = { at: Int, reason: ErrorKind }

/// The effect `read` and `read_template` raise when they reject their input.
pub effect regex {
  /// The text is not a pattern of this dialect, or not a template for its pattern.
  raise fail(e: Error)
}

/// Returns the message that describes an error's reason, which the checker shows when a regex
/// literal in a program fails to compile.
pub fn reason(reason: ErrorKind) -> String =
  match reason {
    UnclosedGroup -> "this `(` has no closing `)`",
    UnopenedGroup -> "this `)` closes nothing: write `\\)` for the character",
    UnclosedClass -> "this class has no closing `]`",
    BadRange -> "a range in a class must run from the lesser character to the greater",
    BadClassName ->
      "no class has this name: write a class name such as `alpha`, as in `[[:alpha:]]`",
    TrailingEscape -> "the pattern ends with a `\\`, which must be followed by a character",
    BadEscape ->
      "this escape means nothing here: `\\` must be followed by a punctuation character or by an escape letter such as `d` in `\\d`",
    NothingToRepeat ->
      "the repeat operator (`*`, `+`, `?` or `{...}`) has nothing before it to repeat",
    NestedRepeat ->
      "a repeat operator applies to one item, not to another repeat: wrap the first repeat in a group `(?:...)`",
    BadRepeat ->
      "a repeat count must be at most 1000, and in a range such as `{2,5}` the first number must not exceed the second",
    BadGroup ->
      "`(?` must be followed by `:`, `P<name>`, `<name>` or flags: the flags are `i`, `m`, `s` and `U`, and also `u` when the pattern matches text",
    BadGroupName ->
      "a group's name must contain only letters, digits and `_`, and must have at least one character",
    DuplicateName -> "another group has this name",
    Backreference ->
      "backreferences are not supported: they can make matching take exponential time",
    Lookaround ->
      "lookahead and lookbehind are not supported: they can make matching take exponential time",
    UnicodeProperty ->
      "no property has this name: `\\p` accepts a Unicode general category, a script, `Alphabetic`, `Lowercase`, `Uppercase`, `White_Space`, `XID_Start`, `XID_Continue` or `Any`, and a pattern that matches bytes accepts none of these",
    HalfCharacter ->
      "`\\C` is not supported in a pattern that matches text: it would match part of a character",
    NotAByte ->
      "a pattern that matches bytes cannot contain a character above U+00FF (255): write a byte as `\\xNN`",
    TooLarge -> "the pattern compiles to more instructions than the limit allows",
    TooDeep -> "groups can nest at most 200 deep",
    LoneDollar ->
      "in replacement text, a `$` must be followed by a group's number or name: write `$$` for a literal `$`",
    UnclosedName -> "this `${` has no closing `}`",
    NoSuchGroup -> "the pattern has no group with this number or name",
  }

fn fail<a>(at: Int, reason: ErrorKind) -> a / {regex.fail} = regex.fail({ at: at, reason: reason })

type Interval = { lo: Int, hi: Int }

type Assertion =
  | LineStart
  | LineEnd
  | TextStart
  | TextEnd
  | WordBoundary
  | NotWordBoundary
  | UnicodeWordBoundary
  | NotUnicodeWordBoundary

type Node =
  | Empty
  | Literal(Int)
  | Class(List<Interval>)
  | Looking(Assertion)
  | Concat(List<Node>)
  | Alternate(List<Node>)
  | Repeat(Node, Int, Int, Bool)
  | Capture(Int, Option<String>, Node)

type Source = { text: Array<Int>, matches_bytes: Bool, limit: Int }

type Parse = { node: Node, size: Int, at: Int, flags: Int, groups: List<Option<String>> }

type Meta =
  | Open
  | Close
  | Bar
  | Star
  | Plus
  | QuestionMark
  | Brace
  | Bracket
  | Backslash
  | Dot
  | Caret
  | Dollar
  | Plain
  | End

fn meta(c: Int) -> Meta =
  match c {
    b'(' -> Open,
    b')' -> Close,
    b'[' -> Bracket,
    b'{' -> Brace,
    b'|' -> Bar,
    b'*' -> Star,
    b'+' -> Plus,
    b'?' -> QuestionMark,
    b'\\' -> Backslash,
    b'.' -> Dot,
    b'^' -> Caret,
    b'$' -> Dollar,
    -1 -> End,
    _ -> Plain,
  }

fn code_point_at(s: Source, at: Int) -> Int = match s.text.at(at) { Some(c) -> c, None -> -1 }

fn max_code_point(s: Source) -> Int = if s.matches_bytes { 0xFF } else { 0x10FFFF }

fn ignores_case(flags: Int) -> Bool = flags & 1 != 0

fn multi_line(flags: Int) -> Bool = flags & 2 != 0

fn dot_all(flags: Int) -> Bool = flags & 4 != 0

fn is_ungreedy(flags: Int) -> Bool = flags & 8 != 0

fn is_unicode(flags: Int) -> Bool = flags & 16 != 0

fn interval(lo: Int, hi: Int) -> Interval = { lo: lo, hi: hi }

fn canonical(items: List<Interval>) -> List<Interval> =
  items.sort_by(|a: Interval, b: Interval| a.lo <= b.lo).fold(
    [],
    |accumulator: List<Interval>, i: Interval|
      match accumulator.at(accumulator.len() - 1) {
        Some(last) if i.lo <= last.hi + 1 ->
          accumulator.set(accumulator.len() - 1, interval(last.lo, max(last.hi, i.hi))),
        _ -> accumulator.push(i),
      },
  )

fn complement(set: List<Interval>, most: Int) -> List<Interval> = {
  let walked = set.fold(
    { next: 0, out: [] },
    |rewrite_case: { next: Int, out: List<Interval> }, i: Interval|
      {
        next: i.hi + 1,
        out: if i.lo > rewrite_case.next {
          rewrite_case.out.push(interval(rewrite_case.next, i.lo - 1))
        } else { rewrite_case.out },
      },
  );
  if walked.next <= most { walked.out.push(interval(walked.next, most)) } else { walked.out }
}

fn folded_ascii(items: List<Interval>) -> List<Interval> =
  items.fold(items, |accumulator: List<Interval>, i: Interval| {
    let lower = if i.lo <= 122 && i.hi >= 97 {
      accumulator.push(interval(max(i.lo, 97) - 32, min(i.hi, 122) - 32))
    } else { accumulator };
    if i.lo <= 90 && i.hi >= 65 { lower.push(interval(max(i.lo, 65) + 32, min(i.hi, 90) + 32)) }
    else { lower }
  })

const case_fold_runs: Array<Int> =
  Array::of_list(
    ucd::runs(embed("ucd/fold.txt")).fold([], |required_literal: List<Int>, run: ucd::Run|
      Bytes::split(match run.fields.at(0) { Some(far) -> far, None -> b"" }, b",").fold(
        required_literal,
        |so_far: List<Int>, far: Bytes|
          so_far.push(run.first).push(run.last).push(ucd::parse_offset(far)),
      )),
  )

fn folded_unicode(items: List<Interval>) -> List<Interval> / {abort.raise} = {
  let runs = case_fold_runs;
  let count = runs.len() / 3;
  items.fold(items, |accumulator: List<Interval>, i: Interval| {
    let from = iterate({ low: 0, high: count }, 32, |s: { low: Int, high: Int }|
      if s.low >= s.high { Stop(s) } else {
        let mid = (s.low + s.high) / 2;
        match runs.at(3 * mid + 1) {
          Some(last) if last < i.lo -> Continue({ low: mid + 1, high: s.high }),
          _ -> Continue({ low: s.low, high: mid }),
        }
      }).low;
    iterate({ at: from, out: accumulator }, count + 1, |s: { at: Int, out: List<Interval> }|
      match ((runs.at(3 * s.at), runs.at(3 * s.at + 1), runs.at(3 * s.at + 2))) {
        (Some(first), Some(last), Some(far)) -> if first > i.hi { Stop(s) } else {
          Continue({
            at: s.at + 1,
            out: s.out.push(
              interval(
                ucd::apply_distance(max(first, i.lo), far),
                ucd::apply_distance(min(last, i.hi), far),
              ),
            ),
          })
        },
        _ -> Stop(s),
      }).out
  })
}

fn folded(items: List<Interval>, bytes: Bool) -> List<Interval> / {abort.raise} =
  if bytes { folded_ascii(items) } else { folded_unicode(items) }

fn digits() -> List<Interval> = [interval(48, 57)]

fn word() -> List<Interval> =
  [interval(48, 57), interval(65, 90), interval(95, 95), interval(97, 122)]

const space: List<Interval> = [interval(9, 10), interval(12, 13), interval(32, 32)]

fn of_property(property: char::Property) -> List<Interval> =
  char::code_point_ranges(property).map(|s: CodePointRange| interval(s.first, s.last))

const unicode_digits: List<Interval> = of_property(char::InCategory(char::DecimalNumber))

const unicode_space: List<Interval> = of_property(char::WhiteSpace)

const unicode_word: List<Interval> =
  canonical(
    [
      of_property(char::Alphabetic),
      of_property(char::InMajorClass(char::Mark)),
      unicode_digits,
      of_property(char::InCategory(char::ConnectorPunctuation)),
      [interval(0x200C, 0x200D)],
    ].flatten(
    ),
  )

fn perl_class(letter: Int, flags: Int) -> Option<List<Interval>> =
  match letter {
    b'd' | b'D' -> Some(if is_unicode(flags) { unicode_digits } else { digits() }),
    b'w' | b'W' -> Some(if is_unicode(flags) { unicode_word } else { word() }),
    b's' | b'S' -> Some(if is_unicode(flags) { unicode_space } else { space }),
    _ -> None,
  }

const scripts: Map<String, List<Interval>> =
  ucd::runs(embed("ucd/scripts.txt")).fold(
    Map::new(),
    |required_literal: Map<String, List<Interval>>, run: ucd::Run| {
      let name = String::of_bytes(match run.fields.at(0) { Some(script) -> script, None -> b"" });
      let so_far = match required_literal.get(name) { Some(found) -> found, None -> [] };
      required_literal.insert(name, so_far.push(interval(run.first, run.last)))
    },
  )

fn named_property(name: String) -> Option<List<Interval>> = {
  let categories = char::categories.filter(|c: char::Category|
    char::abbreviation(c) == name || char::name(c) == name);
  let majors = [
    { short: "L", major: char::Letter },
    { short: "M", major: char::Mark },
    { short: "N", major: char::Number },
    { short: "P", major: char::Punctuation },
    { short: "S", major: char::Symbol },
    { short: "Z", major: char::Separator },
    { short: "C", major: char::Other },
  ].filter(|m: { short: String, major: char::MajorClass }|
    m.short == name || show(m.major) == name);
  match ((categories, majors)) {
    ([category, ..], _) -> Some(of_property(char::InCategory(category))),
    (_, [found, ..]) -> Some(of_property(char::InMajorClass(found.major))),
    _ -> match name {
      "Any" -> Some([interval(0, 0x10FFFF)]),
      "LC" | "Cased_Letter" ->
        Some(
          canonical(
            [
              of_property(char::InCategory(char::UppercaseLetter)),
              of_property(char::InCategory(char::LowercaseLetter)),
              of_property(char::InCategory(char::TitlecaseLetter)),
            ].flatten(
            ),
          ),
        ),
      "Alphabetic" -> Some(of_property(char::Alphabetic)),
      "Lowercase" -> Some(of_property(char::Lowercase)),
      "Uppercase" -> Some(of_property(char::Uppercase)),
      "White_Space" -> Some(of_property(char::WhiteSpace)),
      "XID_Start" -> Some(of_property(char::XidStart)),
      "XID_Continue" -> Some(of_property(char::XidContinue)),
      _ -> scripts.get(name),
    },
  }
}

fn posix_class(name: String) -> Option<List<Interval>> =
  match name {
    "alnum" -> Some([interval(48, 57), interval(65, 90), interval(97, 122)]),
    "alpha" -> Some([interval(65, 90), interval(97, 122)]),
    "ascii" -> Some([interval(0, 127)]),
    "blank" -> Some([interval(9, 9), interval(32, 32)]),
    "cntrl" -> Some([interval(0, 31), interval(127, 127)]),
    "digit" -> Some(digits()),
    "graph" -> Some([interval(33, 126)]),
    "lower" -> Some([interval(97, 122)]),
    "print" -> Some([interval(32, 126)]),
    "punct" -> Some([interval(33, 47), interval(58, 64), interval(91, 96), interval(123, 126)]),
    "space" -> Some([interval(9, 13), interval(32, 32)]),
    "upper" -> Some([interval(65, 90)]),
    "word" -> Some(word()),
    "xdigit" -> Some([interval(48, 57), interval(65, 70), interval(97, 102)]),
    _ -> None,
  }

fn is_name_char(c: Int) -> Bool = is_letter(c) || is_digit(c) || c == 95

fn class_with_flags(
  s: Source,
  set: List<Interval>,
  flags: Int,
  negated: Bool,
) -> List<Interval> / {abort.raise} = {
  let cased = if ignores_case(flags) { canonical(folded(set, s.matches_bytes)) } else { set };
  if negated { complement(cased, max_code_point(s)) } else { cased }
}

fn property(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
) -> { items: List<Interval>, at: Int } / {regex.fail, abort.raise} = {
  let outside = code_point_at(s, at + 1) == b'P';
  let braced = code_point_at(s, at + 2) == b'{';
  let inside = braced && code_point_at(s, at + 3) == b'^';
  let from = if inside { at + 4 } else if braced { at + 3 } else { at + 2 };
  let end = if braced { name_end(s.text, from) }
  else if is_letter(code_point_at(s, from)) { from + 1 }
  else { from };
  if s.matches_bytes || end == from || (braced && code_point_at(s, end) != b'}') {
    fail(at, UnicodeProperty)
  } else {
    match named_property(name_text(s.text, from, end)) {
      Some(set) ->
        {
          items: class_with_flags(s, set, flags, outside != inside),
          at: if braced { end + 1 } else { end },
        },
      None -> fail(at, UnicodeProperty),
    }
  }
}

fn nullable(node: Node) -> Bool =
  match node {
    Empty | Looking(_) -> true,
    Literal(_) | Class(_) -> false,
    Concat(items) -> items.fold(true, |all: Bool, n: Node| all && nullable(n)),
    Alternate(items) -> items.fold(false, |any: Bool, n: Node| any || nullable(n)),
    Repeat(sub, least, _, _) -> least == 0 || nullable(sub),
    Capture(_, _, sub) -> nullable(sub),
  }

fn concat(items: List<Node>) -> Node = match items { [] -> Empty, [one] -> one, _ -> Concat(items) }

fn appended(items: List<Node>, node: Node) -> List<Node> =
  match node {
    Empty -> items,
    Concat(more) -> more.fold(items, |accumulator: List<Node>, n: Node| accumulator.push(n)),
    _ -> items.push(node),
  }

fn alternate(items: List<Node>) -> Node / {abort.raise} =
  match items {
    [] -> panic("an alternation must have at least one branch"),
    [one] -> one,
    _ -> Alternate(items),
  }

fn branched(items: List<Node>, node: Node) -> List<Node> =
  match node {
    Alternate(more) -> more.fold(items, |accumulator: List<Node>, n: Node| accumulator.push(n)),
    _ -> items.push(node),
  }

fn checked_size(s: Source, at: Int, size: Int) -> Int / {regex.fail} =
  if size > s.limit { fail(at, TooLarge) } else { size }

fn leaf(
  s: Source,
  node: Node,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
) -> Parse / {abort.raise} =
  { node: node, size: node_size(s, node), at: at, flags: flags, groups: groups }

fn node_size(s: Source, node: Node) -> Int / {abort.raise} =
  match node {
    Literal(c) -> if s.matches_bytes { 1 } else { utf8_bytes(c).len() },
    Class(set) -> if is_flat(set, s.matches_bytes) { 1 }
    else { class_fragment(set, s.matches_bytes, false).instructions.len() },
    Looking(_) -> 1,
    _ -> 0,
  }

fn alternation(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
  depth: Int,
) -> Parse / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  branches(s, at, flags, groups, depth, [], 0, s.text.len() - at + 1)

fn branches(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
  depth: Int,
  done: List<Node>,
  size: Int,
  left: Int,
) -> Parse / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  if left <= 0 {
    panic(
      "the parser cannot finish: it found more alternatives than there are characters left to read",
    )
  } else {
    let one = sequence(s, at, flags, groups, depth, [], 0, s.text.len() - at + 1);
    let all = branched(done, one.node);
    let total = checked_size(s, at, size + one.size + (if done.len() == 0 { 0 } else { 1 }));
    if meta(code_point_at(s, one.at)) == Bar {
      branches(s, one.at + 1, one.flags, one.groups, depth, all, total, left - 1)
    } else {
      { node: alternate(all), size: total, at: one.at, flags: one.flags, groups: one.groups }
    }
  }

fn sequence(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
  depth: Int,
  items: List<Node>,
  size: Int,
  left: Int,
) -> Parse / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  if left <= 0 {
    panic("the parser cannot finish: it found more pieces than there are characters left to read")
  } else {
    match meta(code_point_at(s, at)) {
      End | Bar | Close ->
        { node: concat(items), size: size, at: at, flags: flags, groups: groups },
      _ -> {
        let p = piece(s, at, flags, groups, depth);
        sequence(
          s,
          p.at,
          p.flags,
          p.groups,
          depth,
          appended(items, p.node),
          checked_size(s, at, size + p.size),
          left - 1,
        )
      },
    }
  }

fn piece(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
  depth: Int,
) -> Parse / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  match meta(code_point_at(s, at)) {
    Star | Plus | QuestionMark -> fail(at, NothingToRepeat),
    Brace -> match repeat_count(s, at + 1) {
      Some(_) -> fail(at, NothingToRepeat),
      None -> repetition(s, leaf(s, Literal(code_point_at(s, at)), at + 1, flags, groups)),
    },
    Open -> repetition(s, parenthesis(s, at, flags, groups, depth)),
    Bracket -> repetition(s, class(s, at, flags, groups)),
    Backslash -> if code_point_at(s, at + 1) == b'Q' { quotation(s, at + 2, flags, groups) }
    else { repetition(s, escape_sequence(s, at, flags, groups)) },
    Dot -> repetition(s, leaf(s, Class(any(s, flags)), at + 1, flags, groups)),
    Caret ->
      repetition(
        s,
        leaf(
          s,
          Looking(if multi_line(flags) { LineStart } else { TextStart }),
          at + 1,
          flags,
          groups,
        ),
      ),
    Dollar ->
      repetition(
        s,
        leaf(s, Looking(if multi_line(flags) { LineEnd } else { TextEnd }), at + 1, flags, groups),
      ),
    _ ->
      repetition(s, leaf(s, character(s, at, code_point_at(s, at), flags), at + 1, flags, groups)),
  }

fn any(s: Source, flags: Int) -> List<Interval> =
  if dot_all(flags) { [interval(0, max_code_point(s))] }
  else { [interval(0, 9), interval(11, max_code_point(s))] }

fn character(s: Source, at: Int, c: Int, flags: Int) -> Node / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  if s.matches_bytes && c > 0xFF { fail(at, NotAByte) }
  else if !ignores_case(flags) { Literal(c) } else {
    match canonical(folded([interval(c, c)], s.matches_bytes)) {
      [only] if only.lo == only.hi -> Literal(c),
      orbit -> Class(orbit),
    }
  }

fn repeat_count(s: Source, at: Int) -> Option<{ minimum_sizes: Int, most: Int, at: Int }> = {
  let first = number(s, at);
  if first.at == at { None } else {
    match code_point_at(s, first.at) {
      b'}' -> Some({ minimum_sizes: first.value, most: first.value, at: first.at + 1 }),
      b',' -> if code_point_at(s, first.at + 1) == b'}' {
        Some({ minimum_sizes: first.value, most: -1, at: first.at + 2 })
      } else {
        let second = number(s, first.at + 1);
        if second.at == first.at + 1 || code_point_at(s, second.at) != b'}' { None }
        else { Some({ minimum_sizes: first.value, most: second.value, at: second.at + 1 }) }
      },
      _ -> None,
    }
  }
}

fn number(s: Source, at: Int) -> { value: Int, at: Int } =
  if !is_digit(code_point_at(s, at))
      || (code_point_at(s, at) == 48 && is_digit(code_point_at(s, at + 1))) { { value: 0, at: at } }
  else { digits_from(s, at, 0) }

fn digits_from(s: Source, at: Int, value: Int) -> { value: Int, at: Int } =
  if at >= s.text.len() || !is_digit(code_point_at(s, at)) { { value: value, at: at } } else {
    digits_from(s, at + 1, if value > 1000 { 1001 } else { value * 10 + code_point_at(s, at) - 48 })
  }

fn repetition(s: Source, p: Parse) -> Parse / {regex.fail} =
  match meta(code_point_at(s, p.at)) {
    Star -> repeat_node(s, p, 0, -1, p.at + 1),
    Plus -> repeat_node(s, p, 1, -1, p.at + 1),
    QuestionMark -> repeat_node(s, p, 0, 1, p.at + 1),
    Brace -> match repeat_count(s, p.at + 1) {
      None -> p,
      Some(c) -> if c.minimum_sizes > 1000 || c.most > 1000
          || (c.most >= 0 && c.minimum_sizes > c.most) { fail(p.at, BadRepeat) }
      else { repeat_node(s, p, c.minimum_sizes, c.most, c.at) },
    },
    _ -> p,
  }

fn repeat_node(s: Source, p: Parse, least: Int, most: Int, at: Int) -> Parse / {regex.fail} = {
  let lazy = meta(code_point_at(s, at)) == QuestionMark;
  let next = if lazy { at + 1 } else { at };
  let stacked = match meta(code_point_at(s, next)) {
    Star | Plus | QuestionMark -> true,
    Brace -> repeat_count(s, next + 1) != None,
    _ -> false,
  };
  if stacked { fail(next, NestedRepeat) } else {
    {
      ..p,
      node: Repeat(p.node, least, most, lazy == is_ungreedy(p.flags)),
      size: checked_size(s, p.at, repeat_size(p.node, p.size, least, most)),
      at: next,
    }
  }
}

fn repeat_size(node: Node, size: Int, least: Int, most: Int) -> Int =
  if most >= 0 { least * size + (most - least) * (size + 1) }
  else if least > 0 { least * size + 1 }
  else if nullable(node) { size + 2 }
  else { size + 1 }

fn quotation(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
) -> Parse / {regex.fail, abort.raise} = {
  let end = quote_end(s, at);
  let after = if end < s.text.len() { end + 2 } else { end };
  if end == at { no_operand(s, after, flags, groups) } else {
    let front = range(at, end - 1).fold(
      { items: [], size: 0 },
      |accumulator: { items: List<Node>, size: Int }, i: Int| {
        let node = character(s, i, code_point_at(s, i), flags);
        { items: accumulator.items.push(node), size: accumulator.size + node_size(s, node) }
      },
    );
    let last = repetition(
      s,
      leaf(s, character(s, end - 1, code_point_at(s, end - 1), flags), after, flags, groups),
    );
    {
      ..last,
      node: concat(appended(front.items, last.node)),
      size: checked_size(s, at, front.size + last.size),
    }
  }
}

fn quote_end(s: Source, at: Int) -> Int =
  if at >= s.text.len() { at }
  else if code_point_at(s, at) == b'\\' && code_point_at(s, at + 1) == b'E' { at }
  else { quote_end(s, at + 1) }

fn escape_sequence(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
) -> Parse / {regex.fail, abort.raise} = {
  let c = code_point_at(s, at + 1);
  match c {
    b'A' -> leaf(s, Looking(TextStart), at + 2, flags, groups),
    b'z' -> leaf(s, Looking(TextEnd), at + 2, flags, groups),
    b'b' ->
      leaf(
        s,
        Looking(if is_unicode(flags) { UnicodeWordBoundary } else { WordBoundary }),
        at + 2,
        flags,
        groups,
      ),
    b'B' ->
      leaf(
        s,
        Looking(if is_unicode(flags) { NotUnicodeWordBoundary } else { NotWordBoundary }),
        at + 2,
        flags,
        groups,
      ),
    b'p' | b'P' -> {
      let named = property(s, at, flags);
      leaf(s, Class(canonical(named.items)), named.at, flags, groups)
    },
    b'k' -> fail(at, Backreference),
    b'C' -> if s.matches_bytes { leaf(s, Class([interval(0, 0xFF)]), at + 2, flags, groups) }
    else { fail(at, HalfCharacter) },
    _ -> match perl_class(c, flags) {
      Some(set) -> leaf(s, Class(class_with_flags(s, set, 0, c < 97)), at + 2, flags, groups),
      None -> {
        let one = escape_code(s, at);
        leaf(s, character(s, at, one.code, flags), one.at, flags, groups)
      },
    },
  }
}

fn escape_code(s: Source, at: Int) -> { code: Int, at: Int } / {regex.fail} = {
  let c = code_point_at(s, at + 1);
  match c {
    -1 -> fail(at, TrailingEscape),
    b'a' -> { code: 7, at: at + 2 },
    b'f' -> { code: 12, at: at + 2 },
    b'n' -> { code: 10, at: at + 2 },
    b'r' -> { code: 13, at: at + 2 },
    b't' -> { code: 9, at: at + 2 },
    b'v' -> { code: 11, at: at + 2 },
    b'0' -> octal(s, at + 2, 0, 2),
    b'1'..=b'9' -> fail(at, Backreference),
    b'x' -> hexadecimal(s, at),
    _ -> if c < 128 && !is_letter(c) { { code: c, at: at + 2 } } else { fail(at, BadEscape) },
  }
}

fn octal(s: Source, at: Int, value: Int, left: Int) -> { code: Int, at: Int } = {
  let c = code_point_at(s, at);
  if left <= 0 || c < 48 || c > 55 { { code: value, at: at } }
  else { octal(s, at + 1, value * 8 + c - 48, left - 1) }
}

fn hexadecimal(s: Source, at: Int) -> { code: Int, at: Int } / {regex.fail} =
  if code_point_at(s, at + 2) == b'{' {
    let read = read_hex_digits(s, at + 3, 0);
    if read.at == at + 3 || code_point_at(s, read.at) != b'}' || read.code > 0x10FFFF {
      fail(at, BadEscape)
    } else { { code: read.code, at: read.at + 1 } }
  } else {
    let high = hex_value(code_point_at(s, at + 2));
    let low = hex_value(code_point_at(s, at + 3));
    if high < 0 || low < 0 { fail(at, BadEscape) } else { { code: high * 16 + low, at: at + 4 } }
  }

fn read_hex_digits(s: Source, at: Int, value: Int) -> { code: Int, at: Int } = {
  let digit = hex_value(code_point_at(s, at));
  if at >= s.text.len() || digit < 0 { { code: value, at: at } }
  else { read_hex_digits(s, at + 1, if value > 0x10FFFF { value } else { value * 16 + digit }) }
}

fn parenthesis(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
  depth: Int,
) -> Parse / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  if depth <= 0 { fail(at, TooDeep) } else if meta(code_point_at(s, at + 1)) != QuestionMark {
    capture(s, at, at + 1, flags, groups, depth - 1, None)
  } else {
    match code_point_at(s, at + 2) {
      b':' -> close_group(s, at, alternation(s, at + 3, flags, groups, depth - 1), flags),
      b'=' | b'!' -> fail(at, Lookaround),
      b'P' -> match code_point_at(s, at + 3) {
        b'<' -> named_group(s, at, at + 4, flags, groups, depth - 1),
        b'=' -> fail(at, Backreference),
        _ -> fail(at, BadGroup),
      },
      b'<' -> match code_point_at(s, at + 3) {
        b'=' | b'!' -> fail(at, Lookaround),
        _ -> named_group(s, at, at + 3, flags, groups, depth - 1),
      },
      _ -> flag_group(s, at, at + 2, flags, flags, false, false, groups, depth - 1),
    }
  }

fn close_group(s: Source, open: Int, inner: Parse, flags: Int) -> Parse / {regex.fail} =
  if meta(code_point_at(s, inner.at)) != Close { fail(open, UnclosedGroup) }
  else { { ..inner, at: inner.at + 1, flags: flags } }

fn capture(
  s: Source,
  open: Int,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
  depth: Int,
  name: Option<String>,
) -> Parse / {regex.fail, abort.raise} = {
  let index = groups.len();
  let inner = close_group(s, open, alternation(s, at, flags, groups.push(name), depth), flags);
  { ..inner, node: Capture(index, name, inner.node), size: checked_size(s, open, inner.size + 2) }
}

fn named_group(
  s: Source,
  open: Int,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
  depth: Int,
) -> Parse / {regex.fail, abort.raise} = {
  let end = name_end(s.text, at);
  if end == at || code_point_at(s, end) != b'>' { fail(at, BadGroupName) } else {
    let name = name_text(s.text, at, end);
    if groups.fold(false, |found: Bool, g: Option<String>| found || g == Some(name)) {
      fail(at, DuplicateName)
    } else { capture(s, open, end + 1, flags, groups, depth, Some(name)) }
  }
}

fn name_end(text: Array<Int>, at: Int) -> Int =
  match text.at(at) { Some(c) if is_name_char(c) -> name_end(text, at + 1), _ -> at }

fn name_text(text: Array<Int>, from: Int, to: Int) -> String / {abort.raise} =
  String::of_bytes(Bytes::concat_all(range(from, to).map(|i: Int| byte_of_int(text.get(i)))))

fn flag_group(
  s: Source,
  open: Int,
  at: Int,
  before: Int,
  on: Int,
  off: Bool,
  seen: Bool,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
  depth: Int,
) -> Parse / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  if at >= s.text.len() { fail(open, UnclosedGroup) } else {
    let c = code_point_at(s, at);
    let bit = match c {
      b'i' -> 1,
      b'm' -> 2,
      b's' -> 4,
      b'U' -> 8,
      b'u' -> if s.matches_bytes { 0 } else { 16 },
      _ -> 0,
    };
    if bit != 0 {
      flag_group(
        s,
        open,
        at + 1,
        before,
        if off { on & ~bit } else { on | bit },
        off,
        true,
        groups,
        depth,
      )
    } else if c == b'-' && !off {
      flag_group(s, open, at + 1, before, on, true, false, groups, depth)
    } else if off && !seen { fail(at, BadGroup) }
    else if c == b':' { close_group(s, open, alternation(s, at + 1, on, groups, depth), before) }
    else if meta(c) == Close { no_operand(s, at + 1, on, groups) }
    else { fail(at, BadGroup) }
  }

fn no_operand(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
) -> Parse / {regex.fail} = {
  let repeats = match meta(code_point_at(s, at)) {
    Star | Plus | QuestionMark -> true,
    Brace -> repeat_count(s, at + 1) != None,
    _ -> false,
  };
  if repeats { fail(at, NothingToRepeat) }
  else { { node: Empty, size: 0, at: at, flags: flags, groups: groups } }
}

fn class(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  groups: List<Option<String>>,
) -> Parse / {regex.fail, abort.raise} = {
  let negated = code_point_at(s, at + 1) == b'^';
  let from = if negated { at + 2 } else { at + 1 };
  let read = read_class_members(s, at, from, flags, [], true, s.text.len() - at + 1);
  let set = canonical(read.items);
  leaf(
    s,
    Class(if negated { complement(set, max_code_point(s)) } else { set }),
    read.at,
    flags,
    groups,
  )
}

fn read_class_members(
  s: Source,
  open: Int,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
  items: List<Interval>,
  first: Bool,
  left: Int,
) -> { items: List<Interval>, at: Int } / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  if left <= 0 {
    panic("the parser cannot finish: it found more members than there are characters left to read")
  } else {
    let c = code_point_at(s, at);
    if c == -1 { fail(open, UnclosedClass) }
    else if c == b']' && !first { { items: items, at: at + 1 } } else {
      let one = member(s, at, flags);
      read_class_members(
        s,
        open,
        one.at,
        flags,
        one.items.fold(items, |accumulator: List<Interval>, i: Interval| accumulator.push(i)),
        false,
        left - 1,
      )
    }
  }

fn member(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
) -> { items: List<Interval>, at: Int } / {regex.fail, abort.raise} = {
  let c = code_point_at(s, at);
  let next = code_point_at(s, at + 1);
  if c == b'[' && next == b':' {
    match posix_at(s, at, flags) { Some(found) -> found, None -> class_range(s, at, flags) }
  } else if c == b'\\' {
    if next == b'p' || next == b'P' { property(s, at, flags) } else {
      match perl_class(next, flags) {
        Some(set) -> { items: class_with_flags(s, set, flags, next < 97), at: at + 2 },
        None -> class_range(s, at, flags),
      }
    }
  } else { class_range(s, at, flags) }
}

fn posix_at(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
) -> Option<{ items: List<Interval>, at: Int }> / {regex.fail, abort.raise} = {
  let negated = code_point_at(s, at + 2) == b'^';
  let from = if negated { at + 3 } else { at + 2 };
  let end = name_end(s.text, from);
  if code_point_at(s, end) != b':' || code_point_at(s, end + 1) != b']' { None } else {
    match posix_class(name_text(s.text, from, end)) {
      Some(set) -> Some({ items: class_with_flags(s, set, flags, negated), at: end + 2 }),
      None -> fail(at, BadClassName),
    }
  }
}

fn class_range(
  s: Source,
  at: Int,
  flags: Int,
) -> { items: List<Interval>, at: Int } / {regex.fail, abort.raise} = {
  let low = class_code(s, at);
  if code_point_at(s, low.at) == b'-' && code_point_at(s, low.at + 1) != b']'
      && code_point_at(s, low.at + 1) != -1 {
    let high = class_code(s, low.at + 1);
    if high.code < low.code { fail(at, BadRange) } else {
      { items: class_with_flags(s, [interval(low.code, high.code)], flags, false), at: high.at }
    }
  } else {
    { items: class_with_flags(s, [interval(low.code, low.code)], flags, false), at: low.at }
  }
}

fn class_code(s: Source, at: Int) -> { code: Int, at: Int } / {regex.fail} = {
  let one = if code_point_at(s, at) == b'\\' { escape_code(s, at) }
  else { { code: code_point_at(s, at), at: at + 1 } };
  if s.matches_bytes && one.code > 0xFF { fail(at, NotAByte) } else { one }
}

fn node_text(node: Node, level: Int, bytes: Bool) -> String / {abort.raise} =
  match node {
    Empty -> "(?:)",
    Literal(c) -> char_text(c, bytes, "\\.+*?()|[]{}^$"),
    Class(set) -> class_text(set, bytes),
    Looking(look) -> match look {
      LineStart -> "(?m:^)",
      LineEnd -> "(?m:$)",
      TextStart -> "\\A",
      TextEnd -> "\\z",
      WordBoundary -> "\\b",
      NotWordBoundary -> "\\B",
      UnicodeWordBoundary -> "(?u:\\b)",
      NotUnicodeWordBoundary -> "(?u:\\B)",
    },
    Concat(items) ->
      bracketed(String::join(items.map(|n: Node| node_text(n, 1, bytes)), ""), level >= 2),
    Alternate(items) ->
      bracketed(String::join(items.map(|n: Node| node_text(n, 0, bytes)), "|"), level >= 1),
    Repeat(sub, least, most, greedy) ->
      bracketed(
        node_text(sub, 2, bytes) ++ count_text(least, most) ++ (if greedy { "" } else { "?" }),
        level >= 2,
      ),
    Capture(_, name, sub) ->
      "(" ++ (match name { Some(n) -> "?P<" ++ n ++ ">", None -> "" }) ++ node_text(sub, 0, bytes)
        ++ ")",
  }

fn bracketed(text: String, wrap: Bool) -> String = if wrap { "(?:" ++ text ++ ")" } else { text }

fn count_text(least: Int, most: Int) -> String =
  if most == -1 { match least { 0 -> "*", 1 -> "+", _ -> "{" ++ least.to_string() ++ ",}" } }
  else if least == 0 && most == 1 { "?" }
  else if least == most { "{" ++ least.to_string() ++ "}" }
  else { "{" ++ least.to_string() ++ "," ++ most.to_string() ++ "}" }

fn char_text(c: Int, bytes: Bool, special: String) -> String / {abort.raise} =
  if c < 32 || c == 127 || (bytes && c > 126) { "\\x{" ++ hex_text(c) ++ "}" } else {
    match Char::of_int(c) {
      None -> "\\x{" ++ hex_text(c) ++ "}",
      Some(ch) -> {
        let text = String::of_chars([ch]);
        if special.contains(text) { "\\" ++ text } else { text }
      },
    }
  }

fn hex_text(n: Int) -> String / {abort.raise} =
  if n < 16 { "0123456789ABCDEF".slice(n, n + 1) }
  else { hex_text(n / 16) ++ "0123456789ABCDEF".slice(n % 16, n % 16 + 1) }

fn class_text(set: List<Interval>, bytes: Bool) -> String / {abort.raise} = {
  let most = if bytes { 0xFF } else { 0x10FFFF };
  if set == [interval(0, most)] { "(?s:.)" } else {
    let negated = set.len() == 0
      || (match set.at(set.len() - 1) { Some(last) -> last.hi == most, None -> false });
    let shown = if negated { complement(set, most) } else { set };
    "[" ++ (if negated { "^" } else { "" })
      ++ String::join(
        shown.map(|i: Interval|
          if i.lo == i.hi { char_text(i.lo, bytes, "\\]^-[") }
          else { char_text(i.lo, bytes, "\\]^-[") ++ "-" ++ char_text(i.hi, bytes, "\\]^-[") }),
        "",
      )
      ++ "]"
  }
}

type Instruction =
  | Range(Int, Int, Int)
  | Switch(Bytes, Array<Int>)
  | Split(Int, Int)
  | Save(Int, Int)
  | Check(Int, Int)
  | Match
  | Fail

type ClassFragment = { instructions: List<Instruction>, entry: Int, cuts: List<Int> }

fn utf8_bytes(c: Int) -> List<Int> =
  if c < 0x80 { [c] }
  else if c < 0x800 { [0xC0 | c >> 6, 0x80 | c & 0x3F] }
  else if c < 0x10000 { [0xE0 | c >> 12, 0x80 | c >> 6 & 0x3F, 0x80 | c & 0x3F] }
  else { [0xF0 | c >> 18, 0x80 | c >> 12 & 0x3F, 0x80 | c >> 6 & 0x3F, 0x80 | c & 0x3F] }

fn sequences(set: List<Interval>, bytes: Bool) -> List<List<Interval>> / {abort.raise} =
  if bytes { set.map(|i: Interval| [i]) } else {
    set.fold([], |accumulator: List<List<Interval>>, i: Interval|
      runs(max(i.lo, 0xE000), i.hi, runs(i.lo, min(i.hi, 0xD7FF), accumulator, 32), 32))
  }

fn runs(
  lo: Int,
  hi: Int,
  done: List<List<Interval>>,
  left: Int,
) -> List<List<Interval>> / {abort.raise} =
  if lo > hi { done } else if left <= 0 {
    panic("a range of code points was split into more ranges than the limit allows")
  } else if lo <= 0x7F && hi > 0x7F { runs(0x80, hi, runs(lo, 0x7F, done, left - 1), left - 1) }
  else if lo <= 0x7FF && hi > 0x7FF { runs(0x800, hi, runs(lo, 0x7FF, done, left - 1), left - 1) }
  else if lo <= 0xFFFF && hi > 0xFFFF {
    runs(0x10000, hi, runs(lo, 0xFFFF, done, left - 1), left - 1)
  } else { split_aligned(lo, hi, 6, done, left - 1) }

fn split_aligned(
  lo: Int,
  hi: Int,
  bits: Int,
  done: List<List<Interval>>,
  left: Int,
) -> List<List<Interval>> / {abort.raise} =
  if bits > 18 || lo < 0x80 { done.push(utf8_sequence(lo, hi)) } else {
    let low = (1 << bits) - 1;
    if lo & ~low == hi & ~low { split_aligned(lo, hi, bits + 6, done, left) }
    else if lo & low != 0 { runs((lo | low) + 1, hi, runs(lo, lo | low, done, left), left) }
    else if hi & low != low { runs(hi & ~low, hi, runs(lo, (hi & ~low) - 1, done, left), left) }
    else { split_aligned(lo, hi, bits + 6, done, left) }
  }

fn utf8_sequence(lo: Int, hi: Int) -> List<Interval> = {
  let high = utf8_bytes(hi);
  utf8_bytes(lo).fold([], |accumulator: List<Interval>, b: Int|
    accumulator.push(interval(b, high.at_or(accumulator.len(), b))))
}

type FragmentBuilder = {
  instructions: List<Instruction>,
  known: Map<List<List<Interval>>, Int>,
  cuts: List<Int>,
}

type BuilderEntry = { building: FragmentBuilder, entry: Int }

type Arm = { first_interval: Interval, place: Int }

fn is_flat(set: List<Interval>, bytes: Bool) -> Bool =
  bytes || (match set.at(set.len() - 1) { Some(last) -> last.hi < 0x80, None -> false })

fn class_fragment(
  set: List<Interval>,
  bytes: Bool,
  reversed: Bool,
) -> ClassFragment / {abort.raise} =
  if is_flat(set, bytes) {
    match set {
      [] -> { instructions: [Fail], entry: 0, cuts: [] },
      [one] -> { instructions: [Range(one.lo, one.hi, -1)], entry: 0, cuts: [one.lo, one.hi + 1] },
      _ -> {
        let low = byte_table(set, 1, 256, []);
        {
          instructions: [Switch(Bytes::concat_all(low.parts), Array::of_list([-1]))],
          entry: 0,
          cuts: low.cuts,
        }
      },
    }
  } else {
    match set.at(set.len() - 1) {
      Some(last) if last.lo <= 0x80 && last.hi == 0x10FFFF ->
        narrowed(if reversed { any_reverse } else { any_forward }, set),
      _ -> build_fragment(set, bytes, reversed),
    }
  }

fn byte_table(
  set: List<Interval>,
  arm: Int,
  size: Int,
  cuts: List<Int>,
) -> { parts: List<Bytes>, cuts: List<Int> } / {abort.raise} = {
  let rewrite_case = set.fold(
    { at: 0, parts: [], cuts: cuts },
    |rewrite_case: { at: Int, parts: List<Bytes>, cuts: List<Int> }, i: Interval|
      if i.lo >= size { rewrite_case } else {
        let hi = min(i.hi, size - 1);
        {
          at: hi + 1,
          parts: rewrite_case.parts.push(run_of(0, i.lo - rewrite_case.at)).push(
            run_of(arm, hi - i.lo + 1),
          ),
          cuts: rewrite_case.cuts.push(i.lo).push(hi + 1),
        }
      },
  );
  { parts: rewrite_case.parts.push(run_of(0, size - rewrite_case.at)), cuts: rewrite_case.cuts }
}

const any_forward: ClassFragment = build_fragment([interval(0, 0x10FFFF)], false, false)

const any_reverse: ClassFragment = build_fragment([interval(0, 0x10FFFF)], false, true)

fn narrowed(every: ClassFragment, set: List<Interval>) -> ClassFragment / {abort.raise} =
  match every.instructions.at(every.entry) {
    Some(Switch(table, arms)) -> {
      let low = byte_table(set, table.at(0), 128, every.cuts);
      {
        instructions: every.instructions.set(
          every.entry,
          Switch(Bytes::concat_all(low.parts.push(table.slice(128, 256))), arms),
        ),
        entry: every.entry,
        cuts: low.cuts,
      }
    },
    _ ->
      panic(
        "the compiled matcher for any character must begin with a `Switch` over the first byte",
      ),
  }

fn build_fragment(
  set: List<Interval>,
  bytes: Bool,
  reversed: Bool,
) -> ClassFragment / {abort.raise} = {
  let forward = sequences(set, bytes);
  let seqs = if reversed { forward.map(|q: List<Interval>| q.reverse()).sort() } else { forward };
  if seqs.len() == 0 { { instructions: [Fail], entry: 0, cuts: [] } } else {
    let made = branch({ instructions: [], known: Map::new(), cuts: [] }, seqs, 4);
    { instructions: made.building.instructions, entry: made.entry, cuts: made.building.cuts }
  }
}

fn branch(
  b: FragmentBuilder,
  seqs: List<List<Interval>>,
  depth: Int,
) -> BuilderEntry / {abort.raise} =
  match b.known.get(seqs) {
    Some(place) -> { building: b, entry: place },
    None -> if depth <= 0 { panic("a character is at most four bytes") } else {
      let armed = group_by_head(seqs).fold(
        { building: b, arms: [] },
        |accumulator: { building: FragmentBuilder, arms: List<Arm> }, g: { head: Interval, tails: List<List<Interval>> }|
          if g.tails.len() == 0 {
            {
              building: accumulator.building,
              arms: accumulator.arms.push({ first_interval: g.head, place: -1 }),
            }
          } else {
            let below = branch(accumulator.building, g.tails, depth - 1);
            {
              building: below.building,
              arms: accumulator.arms.push({ first_interval: g.head, place: below.entry }),
            }
          },
      );
      let made = dispatch(armed.building, armed.arms);
      {
        building: { ..made.building, known: made.building.known.insert(seqs, made.entry) },
        entry: made.entry,
      }
    },
  }

fn group_by_head(
  seqs: List<List<Interval>>,
) -> List<{ head: Interval, tails: List<List<Interval>> }> =
  seqs.fold(
    [],
    |accumulator: List<{ head: Interval, tails: List<List<Interval>> }>, q: List<Interval>|
      match q {
        [] -> accumulator,
        [head, ..rest] -> match accumulator.at(accumulator.len() - 1) {
          Some(last) if last.head == head && rest.len() == 0 && last.tails.len() == 0 ->
            accumulator,
          Some(last) if last.head == head && rest.len() > 0 && last.tails.len() > 0 ->
            accumulator.set(accumulator.len() - 1, { head: head, tails: last.tails.push(rest) }),
          _ -> accumulator.push({ head: head, tails: if rest.len() == 0 { [] } else { [rest] } }),
        },
      },
  )

fn dispatch(b: FragmentBuilder, arms: List<Arm>) -> BuilderEntry / {abort.raise} = {
  let cut = {
    ..b,
    cuts: arms.fold(b.cuts, |cs: List<Int>, a: Arm|
      cs.push(a.first_interval.lo).push(a.first_interval.hi + 1)),
  };
  let sorted = arms.sort_by(|x: Arm, y: Arm| x.first_interval.lo <= y.first_interval.lo);
  let apart = sorted.fold(
    { ok: true, next: 0 },
    |rewrite_case: { ok: Bool, next: Int }, a: Arm|
      {
        ok: rewrite_case.ok && a.first_interval.lo >= rewrite_case.next,
        next: a.first_interval.hi + 1,
      },
  ).ok;
  match sorted {
    [one] -> add_instruction(cut, Range(one.first_interval.lo, one.first_interval.hi, one.place)),
    _ -> if apart { add_instruction(cut, switch(sorted)) } else {
      arms.reverse().fold({ building: cut, entry: -2 }, |accumulator: BuilderEntry, a: Arm| {
        let one = add_instruction(
          accumulator.building,
          Range(a.first_interval.lo, a.first_interval.hi, a.place),
        );
        if accumulator.entry == -2 { one }
        else { add_instruction(one.building, Split(one.entry, accumulator.entry)) }
      })
    },
  }
}

fn add_instruction(b: FragmentBuilder, instruction: Instruction) -> BuilderEntry =
  { building: { ..b, instructions: b.instructions.push(instruction) }, entry: b.instructions.len() }

fn switch(arms: List<Arm>) -> Instruction / {abort.raise} = {
  let places = arms.map(|a: Arm| a.place).unique();
  let filled = arms.fold(
    { at: 0, parts: [] },
    |rewrite_case: { at: Int, parts: List<Bytes> }, a: Arm| {
      let arm = match places.index_of(a.place) { Some(i) -> i + 1, None -> 0 };
      {
        at: a.first_interval.hi + 1,
        parts: rewrite_case.parts.push(run_of(0, a.first_interval.lo - rewrite_case.at)).push(
          run_of(arm, a.first_interval.hi - a.first_interval.lo + 1),
        ),
      }
    },
  );
  Switch(Bytes::concat_all(filled.parts.push(run_of(0, 256 - filled.at))), Array::of_list(places))
}

fn run_of(b: Int, n: Int) -> Bytes / {abort.raise} =
  if n <= 0 { b"" }
  else if n == 1 { byte_of_int(b) } else {
    let half = run_of(b, n / 2);
    if n % 2 == 0 { half ++ half } else { half ++ half ++ byte_of_int(b) }
  }

type Emitter = {
  instructions: List<Instruction>,
  boundaries: Map<Int, Unit>,
  classes: Map<List<Interval>, ClassFragment>,
  bytes: Bool,
  reversed: Bool,
}

type EmitResult = { emitter: Emitter, entry: Int }

fn emit_instruction(e: Emitter, instruction: Instruction) -> EmitResult =
  { emitter: { ..e, instructions: e.instructions.push(instruction) }, entry: e.instructions.len() }

fn fork(first: Int, other: Int, greedy: Bool) -> Instruction =
  if greedy { Split(first, other) } else { Split(other, first) }

fn look_bits(look: Assertion, reversed: Bool) -> Int =
  match look {
    LineStart -> if reversed { 2 } else { 1 },
    LineEnd -> if reversed { 1 } else { 2 },
    TextStart -> if reversed { 8 } else { 4 },
    TextEnd -> if reversed { 4 } else { 8 },
    WordBoundary -> 16,
    NotWordBoundary -> 32,
    UnicodeWordBoundary -> 64,
    NotUnicodeWordBoundary -> 128,
  }

fn emit(e: Emitter, node: Node, next: Int, depth: Int) -> EmitResult / {abort.raise} =
  if depth <= 0 {
    panic(
      "a parsed pattern cannot nest deeper than its number of parenthesized groups, but this one does",
    )
  } else {
    match node {
      Empty -> { emitter: e, entry: next },
      Literal(c) -> emit_literal(e, c, next),
      Class(set) -> emit_class(e, set, next),
      Looking(look) -> emit_instruction(e, Check(look_bits(look, e.reversed), next)),
      Concat(items) ->
        List::fold(
          if e.reversed { items } else { items.reverse() },
          { emitter: e, entry: next },
          |accumulator: EmitResult, n: Node|
            emit(accumulator.emitter, n, accumulator.entry, depth - 1),
        ),
      Alternate(items) -> {
        let arms = items.fold(
          { e: e, entries: [] },
          |accumulator: { e: Emitter, entries: List<Int> }, n: Node| {
            let one = emit(accumulator.e, n, next, depth - 1);
            { e: one.emitter, entries: accumulator.entries.push(one.entry) }
          },
        );
        arms.entries.reverse().fold(
          { emitter: arms.e, entry: -1 },
          |accumulator: EmitResult, entry: Int|
            if accumulator.entry < 0 { { emitter: accumulator.emitter, entry: entry } }
            else { emit_instruction(accumulator.emitter, Split(entry, accumulator.entry)) },
        )
      },
      Capture(index, _, sub) -> if e.reversed { emit(e, sub, next, depth - 1) } else {
        let epsilon_closure = emit_instruction(e, Save(2 * index + 1, next));
        let body = emit(epsilon_closure.emitter, sub, epsilon_closure.entry, depth - 1);
        emit_instruction(body.emitter, Save(2 * index, body.entry))
      },
      Repeat(sub, least, most, greedy) -> if most >= 0 {
        let tail = optional(e, sub, greedy, next, next, most - least, depth - 1);
        copies(tail.emitter, sub, tail.entry, least, depth - 1)
      } else if least == 0 { star(e, sub, greedy, next, depth - 1) } else {
        let last = plus(e, sub, greedy, next, depth - 1);
        copies(last.emitter, sub, last.entry, least - 1, depth - 1)
      },
    }
  }

fn emit_literal(e: Emitter, c: Int, next: Int) -> EmitResult =
  if !e.bytes && c >= 0xD800 && c <= 0xDFFF { emit_instruction(e, Fail) } else {
    let bytes = if e.bytes { [c] } else { utf8_bytes(c) };
    List::fold(
      if e.reversed { bytes } else { bytes.reverse() },
      { emitter: e, entry: next },
      |accumulator: EmitResult, b: Int|
        emit_instruction(
          {
            ..accumulator.emitter,
            boundaries: accumulator.emitter.boundaries.insert(b, ()).insert(b + 1, ()),
          },
          Range(b, b, accumulator.entry),
        ),
    )
  }

fn emit_class(e: Emitter, set: List<Interval>, next: Int) -> EmitResult / {abort.raise} = {
  let known = e.classes.get(set);
  let t = match known { Some(t) -> t, None -> class_fragment(set, e.bytes, e.reversed) };
  let base = e.instructions.len();
  let instructions = t.instructions.fold(
    e.instructions,
    |accumulator: List<Instruction>, i: Instruction| accumulator.push(relocate(i, base, next)),
  );
  {
    emitter: match known {
      Some(_) -> { ..e, instructions: instructions },
      None ->
        {
          ..e,
          instructions: instructions,
          classes: e.classes.insert(set, t),
          boundaries: t.cuts.fold(e.boundaries, |cuts: Map<Int, Unit>, c: Int| cuts.insert(c, ())),
        },
    },
    entry: base + t.entry,
  }
}

fn relocate(i: Instruction, base: Int, next: Int) -> Instruction =
  match i {
    Range(lo, hi, to) -> Range(lo, hi, if to < 0 { next } else { base + to }),
    Switch(table, arms) ->
      Switch(
        table,
        Array::of_list(arms.to_list().map(|to: Int| if to < 0 { next } else { base + to })),
      ),
    Split(x, y) -> Split(if x < 0 { next } else { base + x }, if y < 0 { next } else { base + y }),
    other -> other,
  }

fn star(e: Emitter, sub: Node, greedy: Bool, next: Int, depth: Int) -> EmitResult / {abort.raise} =
  if nullable(sub) {
    let more = plus(e, sub, greedy, next, depth);
    emit_instruction(more.emitter, fork(more.entry, next, greedy))
  } else {
    let hole = emit_instruction(e, Fail);
    let body = emit(hole.emitter, sub, hole.entry, depth);
    {
      emitter: {
        ..body.emitter,
        instructions: body.emitter.instructions.set(hole.entry, fork(body.entry, next, greedy)),
      },
      entry: hole.entry,
    }
  }

fn plus(e: Emitter, sub: Node, greedy: Bool, next: Int, depth: Int) -> EmitResult / {abort.raise} = {
  let hole = emit_instruction(e, Fail);
  let body = emit(hole.emitter, sub, hole.entry, depth);
  {
    emitter: {
      ..body.emitter,
      instructions: body.emitter.instructions.set(hole.entry, fork(body.entry, next, greedy)),
    },
    entry: body.entry,
  }
}

fn optional(
  e: Emitter,
  sub: Node,
  greedy: Bool,
  next: Int,
  tail: Int,
  count: Int,
  depth: Int,
) -> EmitResult / {abort.raise} =
  if count <= 0 { { emitter: e, entry: tail } } else {
    let body = emit(e, sub, tail, depth);
    let fork = emit_instruction(body.emitter, fork(body.entry, next, greedy));
    optional(fork.emitter, sub, greedy, next, fork.entry, count - 1, depth)
  }

fn copies(e: Emitter, sub: Node, next: Int, count: Int, depth: Int) -> EmitResult / {abort.raise} =
  if count <= 0 { { emitter: e, entry: next } } else {
    let one = emit(e, sub, next, depth);
    copies(one.emitter, sub, one.entry, count - 1, depth)
  }

fn anchored(node: Node) -> Bool =
  match node {
    Looking(TextStart) -> true,
    Concat(items) -> match items { [first, ..] -> anchored(first), [] -> false },
    Alternate(items) -> items.fold(true, |all: Bool, n: Node| all && anchored(n)),
    Repeat(sub, least, _, _) -> least > 0 && anchored(sub),
    Capture(_, _, sub) -> anchored(sub),
    _ -> false,
  }

fn looks_of(node: Node) -> Int =
  match node {
    Looking(look) -> look_bits(look, false),
    Concat(items) | Alternate(items) -> items.fold(0, |all: Int, n: Node| all | looks_of(n)),
    Repeat(sub, _, _, _) | Capture(_, _, sub) -> looks_of(sub),
    _ -> 0,
  }

fn byte_classes(cuts: Map<Int, Unit>) -> { classes: Bytes, count: Int } / {abort.raise} = {
  let rewrite_case = cuts.keys().fold(
    { at: 0, id: 0, parts: [] },
    |rewrite_case: { at: Int, id: Int, parts: List<Bytes> }, c: Int|
      if c <= rewrite_case.at || c > 255 { rewrite_case } else {
        {
          at: c,
          id: rewrite_case.id + 1,
          parts: rewrite_case.parts.push(run_of(rewrite_case.id, c - rewrite_case.at)),
        }
      },
  );
  {
    classes: Bytes::concat_all(
      rewrite_case.parts.push(run_of(rewrite_case.id, 256 - rewrite_case.at)),
    ),
    count: rewrite_case.id + 1,
  }
}

type Prefilter = { first: Bytes, prefix: Bytes, exact: Bool, required: Bytes }

fn prefilter(
  instructions: Array<Instruction>,
  start: Int,
  tree: Node,
  bytes: Bool,
) -> Prefilter / {abort.raise} = {
  let n = instructions.len();
  let led = prefix_from(instructions, start, [], n + 1);
  let firsts = first_from(
    instructions,
    Array::new(n, false),
    Array::new(2 * n + 2, 0).set(0, start),
    1,
    [],
    4 * n + 4,
  );
  let first = match firsts { Some(parts) -> Bytes::concat_all(parts), None -> b"" };
  let lead = Bytes::concat_all(led.bytes);
  let inside = required_literal(tree, bytes);
  {
    first: if first.len() >= 256 { b"" } else { first },
    prefix: lead,
    exact: led.whole,
    required: if inside == lead { b"" } else { inside },
  }
}

fn required_literal(node: Node, bytes: Bool) -> Bytes / {abort.raise} =
  match node {
    Literal(c) -> code_point_bytes(c, bytes),
    Capture(_, _, sub) -> required_literal(sub, bytes),
    Repeat(sub, least, _, _) -> if least > 0 { required_literal(sub, bytes) } else { b"" },
    Concat(items) -> {
      let rewrite_case = items.fold(
        { run: [], best: b"" },
        |rewrite_case: { run: List<Bytes>, best: Bytes }, n: Node|
          match n {
            Literal(c) ->
              { run: rewrite_case.run.push(code_point_bytes(c, bytes)), best: rewrite_case.best },
            _ ->
              {
                run: [],
                best: longer(
                  longer(rewrite_case.best, Bytes::concat_all(rewrite_case.run)),
                  required_literal(n, bytes),
                ),
              },
          },
      );
      longer(rewrite_case.best, Bytes::concat_all(rewrite_case.run))
    },
    _ -> b"",
  }

fn code_point_bytes(c: Int, bytes: Bool) -> Bytes / {abort.raise} =
  if bytes { byte_of_int(c) } else { Bytes::concat_all(utf8_bytes(c).map(|b: Int| byte_of_int(b))) }

fn longer(a: Bytes, b: Bytes) -> Bytes = if b.len() > a.len() { b } else { a }

fn prefix_from(
  instructions: Array<Instruction>,
  pc: Int,
  bytes: List<Bytes>,
  left: Int,
) -> { bytes: List<Bytes>, whole: Bool } / {abort.raise} =
  if left <= 0 { { bytes: bytes, whole: false } } else {
    match instructions.get(pc) {
      Save(_, to) -> prefix_from(instructions, to, bytes, left - 1),
      Range(lo, hi, to) if lo == hi ->
        prefix_from(instructions, to, bytes.push(byte_of_int(lo)), left - 1),
      Match -> { bytes: bytes, whole: true },
      _ -> { bytes: bytes, whole: false },
    }
  }

fn first_from(
  instructions: Array<Instruction>,
  seen: Array<Bool>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  stack_size: Int,
  parts: List<Bytes>,
  left: Int,
) -> Option<List<Bytes>> / {abort.raise} =
  if stack_size <= 0 { Some(parts) } else if left <= 0 {
    panic(
      "the search visited the same step of the compiled pattern twice, but it must visit each step at most once",
    )
  } else {
    let pc = stack.get(stack_size - 1);
    if seen.get(pc) { first_from(instructions, seen, stack, stack_size - 1, parts, left - 1) }
    else {
      let marked = seen.set(pc, true);
      match instructions.get(pc) {
        Split(x, y) ->
          first_from(
            instructions,
            marked,
            stack.set(stack_size - 1, y).set(stack_size, x),
            stack_size + 1,
            parts,
            left - 1,
          ),
        Save(_, to) ->
          first_from(
            instructions,
            marked,
            stack.set(stack_size - 1, to),
            stack_size,
            parts,
            left - 1,
          ),
        Range(lo, hi, _) ->
          first_from(
            instructions,
            marked,
            stack,
            stack_size - 1,
            parts.push(every_byte.slice(lo, hi + 1)),
            left - 1,
          ),
        Switch(table, _) ->
          first_from(
            instructions,
            marked,
            stack,
            stack_size - 1,
            switch_bytes(table, 0, parts, 257),
            left - 1,
          ),
        Fail -> first_from(instructions, marked, stack, stack_size - 1, parts, left - 1),
        Match | Check(_, _) -> None,
      }
    }
  }

fn switch_bytes(
  table: Bytes,
  at: Int,
  parts: List<Bytes>,
  left: Int,
) -> List<Bytes> / {abort.raise} =
  if at >= 256 || left <= 0 { parts } else {
    let from = table.scan(at, b"\x00", 256 - at);
    if from >= 256 { parts } else {
      let to = table.scan_until(from, b"\x00", 256 - from);
      switch_bytes(table, to, parts.push(every_byte.slice(from, to)), left - 1)
    }
  }

const every_byte: Bytes = Bytes::concat_all(range(0, 256).map(|b: Int| byte_of_int(b)))

/// How a pattern is compiled and searched.
pub type Options = {
  /// Whether the match taken at the leftmost start is the longest one there, as in POSIX. Otherwise
  /// it is the one a backtracking search would find first, as in Perl.
  longest: Bool,
  /// The most instructions the pattern may compile to, with every counted repetition written out. A
  /// value above 16777216 is treated as 16777216. A pattern over the limit is rejected as
  /// `TooLarge`. The program that reads a match backwards is built from the same tree and is not
  /// counted.
  size_limit: Int,
  /// The most states that a search caches of the automaton it builds as it reads. A search that
  /// would cache more continues by following every state at once, which costs more per byte and
  /// caches nothing.
  state_limit: Int,
  /// A subject of at most this many bytes is short, and is searched by following every state at
  /// once from the start: a short search meets few states twice, so caching them costs more than it
  /// saves. With a negative number, no subject is short.
  short: Int,
}

/// The default options: the first match a backtracking search would find, 100000 instructions, 4096
/// states, and subjects of 32 bytes or fewer treated as short.
pub const options: Options = { longest: false, size_limit: 100000, state_limit: 4096, short: 32 }

type Automaton = {
  instructions: Array<Instruction>,
  entry: Int,
  classes: Bytes,
  stride: Int,
  first_wins: Bool,
  lines: Bool,
  words: Bool,
}

type Compiled = {
  pattern: String,
  options: Options,
  matches_bytes: Bool,
  tree: Node,
  names: List<Option<String>>,
  numbers: Map<String, Int>,
  instructions: Array<Instruction>,
  start: Int,
  search: Int,
  prefilter: Prefilter,
  finder: Automaton,
  longest_finder: Automaton,
  reverse: Automaton,
  wide: Bool,
}

fn compiled(pattern: String, o: Options, bytes: Bool) -> Compiled / {regex.fail, abort.raise} = {
  let s = {
    text: Array::of_list(pattern.code_points()),
    matches_bytes: bytes,
    limit: max(0, min(o.size_limit, 0x1000000)),
  };
  let p = alternation(s, 0, 0, [None], 200);
  if p.at < s.text.len() { fail(p.at, UnopenedGroup) } else {
    let ahead = emit(
      {
        instructions: [Match],
        boundaries: Map::new(),
        classes: Map::new(),
        bytes: bytes,
        reversed: false,
      },
      Capture(0, None, p.node),
      0,
      1000,
    );
    let sought = if anchored(p.node) { ahead } else {
      let hole = emit_instruction(ahead.emitter, Fail);
      let skip = emit_class(hole.emitter, [interval(0, max_code_point(s))], hole.entry);
      {
        emitter: {
          ..skip.emitter,
          instructions: skip.emitter.instructions.set(hole.entry, Split(ahead.entry, skip.entry)),
        },
        entry: hole.entry,
      }
    };
    let behind = emit(
      {
        instructions: [Match],
        boundaries: sought.emitter.boundaries,
        classes: Map::new(),
        bytes: bytes,
        reversed: true,
      },
      p.node,
      0,
      1000,
    );
    let looks = looks_of(p.node);
    let lined = if looks & 3 != 0 { behind.emitter.boundaries.insert(10, ()).insert(11, ()) }
    else { behind.emitter.boundaries };
    let cuts = if looks & 48 != 0 {
      [48, 58, 65, 91, 95, 96, 97, 123].fold(lined, |cuts: Map<Int, Unit>, c: Int|
        cuts.insert(c, ()))
    } else { lined };
    let class_table = byte_classes(cuts);
    let instructions = Array::of_list(sought.emitter.instructions);
    let finder = {
      instructions: instructions,
      entry: sought.entry,
      classes: class_table.classes,
      stride: class_table.count + 1,
      first_wins: true,
      lines: looks & 3 != 0,
      words: looks & 48 != 0,
    };
    {
      pattern: pattern,
      options: o,
      matches_bytes: bytes,
      tree: p.node,
      names: p.groups,
      numbers: range(0, p.groups.len()).fold(Map::new(), |m: Map<String, Int>, i: Int|
        match p.groups.at(i) { Some(Some(name)) -> m.insert(name, i), _ -> m }),
      instructions: instructions,
      start: ahead.entry,
      search: sought.entry,
      prefilter: prefilter(instructions, ahead.entry, p.node, bytes),
      finder: finder,
      longest_finder: { ..finder, entry: ahead.entry, first_wins: false },
      reverse: {
        ..finder,
        instructions: Array::of_list(behind.emitter.instructions),
        entry: behind.entry,
        first_wins: false,
      },
      wide: looks & 192 != 0,
    }
  }
}

type Run = {
  instructions: Array<Instruction>,
  hay: Bytes,
  stop: Int,
  slots: Int,
  longest: Bool,
  wide: Bool,
}

fn is_word(b: Int) -> Bool =
  (b >= 48 && b <= 57) || (b >= 65 && b <= 90) || b == 95 || (b >= 97 && b <= 122)

fn unicode_word_from(hay: Bytes, at: Int) -> Bool / {abort.raise} =
  if at >= hay.len() { false } else {
    let b = hay.at(at);
    let next = |i: Int| if at + i < hay.len() { hay.at(at + i) & 0x3F } else { 0 };
    let code_point = if b < 0x80 { b }
    else if b < 0xE0 { (b & 0x1F) << 6 | next(1) }
    else if b < 0xF0 { (b & 0x0F) << 12 | next(1) << 6 | next(2) }
    else { (b & 0x07) << 18 | next(1) << 12 | next(2) << 6 | next(3) };
    if code_point < 0x80 { is_word(code_point) } else {
      match Char::of_int(code_point) {
        None -> false,
        Some(c) ->
          c.is_alphabetic() || c.is_mark() || c.is_digit()
            || c.general_category() == char::ConnectorPunctuation
            || code_point == 0x200C
            || code_point == 0x200D,
      }
    }
  }

fn unicode_word_until(hay: Bytes, at: Int) -> Bool / {abort.raise} =
  at > 0
    && unicode_word_from(
      hay,
      [1, 2, 3].fold(at - 1, |start: Int, _: Int|
        if start > 0 && hay.at(start) & 0xC0 == 0x80 { start - 1 } else { start }),
    )

fn looks_at(hay: Bytes, at: Int, is_unicode: Bool) -> Int / {abort.raise} = {
  let n = hay.len();
  let before = if at > 0 { hay.at(at - 1) } else { -1 };
  let after = if at < n { hay.at(at) } else { -1 };
  (if at == 0 { 5 } else if before == 10 { 1 } else { 0 })
    | (if at == n { 10 } else if after == 10 { 2 } else { 0 })
    | (if is_word(before) != is_word(after) { 16 } else { 32 })
    | (if !is_unicode { 0 }
    else if unicode_word_until(hay, at) != unicode_word_from(hay, at) { 64 }
    else { 128 })
}

fn run(r: Run, entry: Int, from: Int) -> Array<Int> / {abort.raise} = {
  let n = r.instructions.len();
  let none = Array::new(0, 0);
  threads_add(
    r,
    (r.stop - from + 2) * (6 * n + 8),
    from - 1,
    Array::new(n, -1),
    Array::new(2 * n + 2, 0).set(0, entry),
    Array::new(2 * n + 2, none).set(0, Array::new(r.slots, -1)),
    1,
    Array::new(n, 0),
    Array::new(n, none),
    0,
    0,
    Array::new(n, 0),
    Array::new(n, none),
    0,
    none,
  )
}

fn threads_step(
  r: Run,
  fuel: Int,
  position: Int,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack_pcs: Array<Int>,
  stack_captures: Array<Array<Int>>,
  stack_size: Int,
  current_pcs: Array<Int>,
  current_captures: Array<Array<Int>>,
  current_count: Int,
  t: Int,
  next_pcs: Array<Int>,
  next_captures: Array<Array<Int>>,
  next_count: Int,
  best: Array<Int>,
) -> Array<Int> / {abort.raise} =
  if fuel <= 0 { panic("a run takes a bounded number of steps") } else if t >= current_count {
    if position >= r.stop || next_count == 0 { best } else {
      threads_step(
        r,
        fuel - 1,
        position + 1,
        seen,
        stack_pcs,
        stack_captures,
        0,
        next_pcs,
        next_captures,
        next_count,
        0,
        current_pcs,
        current_captures,
        0,
        best,
      )
    }
  } else {
    let cap = current_captures.get(t);
    if r.longest && best.len() > 0 && (cap.get(0) < 0 || cap.get(0) > best.get(0)) {
      threads_step(
        r,
        fuel - 1,
        position,
        seen,
        stack_pcs,
        stack_captures,
        stack_size,
        current_pcs,
        current_captures,
        current_count,
        t + 1,
        next_pcs,
        next_captures,
        next_count,
        best,
      )
    } else {
      match r.instructions.get(current_pcs.get(t)) {
        Range(lo, hi, to) -> {
          let b = if position < r.stop { r.hay.at(position) } else { -1 };
          if b >= lo && b <= hi {
            threads_add(
              r,
              fuel - 1,
              position,
              seen,
              stack_pcs.set(0, to),
              stack_captures.set(0, cap),
              1,
              current_pcs,
              current_captures,
              current_count,
              t,
              next_pcs,
              next_captures,
              next_count,
              best,
            )
          } else {
            threads_step(
              r,
              fuel - 1,
              position,
              seen,
              stack_pcs,
              stack_captures,
              stack_size,
              current_pcs,
              current_captures,
              current_count,
              t + 1,
              next_pcs,
              next_captures,
              next_count,
              best,
            )
          }
        },
        Switch(table, arms) -> {
          let arm = if position < r.stop { table.at(r.hay.at(position)) } else { 0 };
          if arm > 0 {
            threads_add(
              r,
              fuel - 1,
              position,
              seen,
              stack_pcs.set(0, arms.get(arm - 1)),
              stack_captures.set(0, cap),
              1,
              current_pcs,
              current_captures,
              current_count,
              t,
              next_pcs,
              next_captures,
              next_count,
              best,
            )
          } else {
            threads_step(
              r,
              fuel - 1,
              position,
              seen,
              stack_pcs,
              stack_captures,
              stack_size,
              current_pcs,
              current_captures,
              current_count,
              t + 1,
              next_pcs,
              next_captures,
              next_count,
              best,
            )
          }
        },
        Match -> if r.longest {
          threads_step(
            r,
            fuel - 1,
            position,
            seen,
            stack_pcs,
            stack_captures,
            stack_size,
            current_pcs,
            current_captures,
            current_count,
            t + 1,
            next_pcs,
            next_captures,
            next_count,
            if best.len() == 0 || cap.get(1) > best.get(1) { cap } else { best },
          )
        } else {
          threads_step(
            r,
            fuel - 1,
            position,
            seen,
            stack_pcs,
            stack_captures,
            stack_size,
            current_pcs,
            current_captures,
            current_count,
            current_count,
            next_pcs,
            next_captures,
            next_count,
            cap,
          )
        },
        _ ->
          threads_step(
            r,
            fuel - 1,
            position,
            seen,
            stack_pcs,
            stack_captures,
            stack_size,
            current_pcs,
            current_captures,
            current_count,
            t + 1,
            next_pcs,
            next_captures,
            next_count,
            best,
          ),
      }
    }
  }

fn threads_add(
  r: Run,
  fuel: Int,
  position: Int,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack_pcs: Array<Int>,
  stack_captures: Array<Array<Int>>,
  stack_size: Int,
  current_pcs: Array<Int>,
  current_captures: Array<Array<Int>>,
  current_count: Int,
  t: Int,
  next_pcs: Array<Int>,
  next_captures: Array<Array<Int>>,
  next_count: Int,
  best: Array<Int>,
) -> Array<Int> / {abort.raise} =
  if fuel <= 0 { panic("a run takes a bounded number of steps") } else if stack_size <= 0 {
    threads_step(
      r,
      fuel - 1,
      position,
      seen,
      stack_pcs,
      stack_captures,
      0,
      current_pcs,
      current_captures,
      current_count,
      t + 1,
      next_pcs,
      next_captures,
      next_count,
      best,
    )
  } else {
    let pc = stack_pcs.get(stack_size - 1);
    if seen.get(pc) == position + 1 {
      threads_add(
        r,
        fuel - 1,
        position,
        seen,
        stack_pcs,
        stack_captures,
        stack_size - 1,
        current_pcs,
        current_captures,
        current_count,
        t,
        next_pcs,
        next_captures,
        next_count,
        best,
      )
    } else {
      let cap = stack_captures.get(stack_size - 1);
      let marked = seen.set(pc, position + 1);
      match r.instructions.get(pc) {
        Split(x, y) ->
          threads_add(
            r,
            fuel - 1,
            position,
            marked,
            stack_pcs.set(stack_size - 1, y).set(stack_size, x),
            stack_captures.set(stack_size, cap),
            stack_size + 1,
            current_pcs,
            current_captures,
            current_count,
            t,
            next_pcs,
            next_captures,
            next_count,
            best,
          ),
        Save(slot, to) ->
          threads_add(
            r,
            fuel - 1,
            position,
            marked,
            stack_pcs.set(stack_size - 1, to),
            if slot < r.slots { stack_captures.set(stack_size - 1, cap.set(slot, position + 1)) }
            else { stack_captures },
            stack_size,
            current_pcs,
            current_captures,
            current_count,
            t,
            next_pcs,
            next_captures,
            next_count,
            best,
          ),
        Check(looks, to) -> if looks & ~looks_at(r.hay, position + 1, r.wide) == 0 {
          threads_add(
            r,
            fuel - 1,
            position,
            marked,
            stack_pcs.set(stack_size - 1, to),
            stack_captures,
            stack_size,
            current_pcs,
            current_captures,
            current_count,
            t,
            next_pcs,
            next_captures,
            next_count,
            best,
          )
        } else {
          threads_add(
            r,
            fuel - 1,
            position,
            marked,
            stack_pcs,
            stack_captures,
            stack_size - 1,
            current_pcs,
            current_captures,
            current_count,
            t,
            next_pcs,
            next_captures,
            next_count,
            best,
          )
        },
        Fail ->
          threads_add(
            r,
            fuel - 1,
            position,
            marked,
            stack_pcs,
            stack_captures,
            stack_size - 1,
            current_pcs,
            current_captures,
            current_count,
            t,
            next_pcs,
            next_captures,
            next_count,
            best,
          ),
        _ ->
          threads_add(
            r,
            fuel - 1,
            position,
            marked,
            stack_pcs,
            stack_captures,
            stack_size - 1,
            current_pcs,
            current_captures,
            current_count,
            t,
            next_pcs.set(next_count, pc),
            next_captures.set(next_count, cap),
            next_count + 1,
            best,
          ),
      }
    }
  }

type States = {
  ids: Map<List<Int>, Int>,
  keys: List<List<Int>>,
  starts: List<Int>,
  room: Int,
  base: Int,
}

type SearchCache = { stamp: Int, ahead: States, back: States, stretch: States, overflowed: Bool }

fn empty_states(room: Int, base: Int) -> States =
  { ids: Map::new(), keys: [[], []], starts: [-1, -1, -1, -1], room: room + 2, base: base }

const empty_search_cache: SearchCache =
  {
    stamp: 1,
    ahead: empty_states(0, 0),
    back: empty_states(0, 0),
    stretch: empty_states(0, 0),
    overflowed: false,
  }

type Closure = {
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  out: List<Int>,
  asked_looks: Int,
  sealed: Bool,
}

fn epsilon_closure(
  instructions: Array<Instruction>,
  have: Int,
  cut: Bool,
  stamp: Int,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  stack_size: Int,
  out: List<Int>,
  needs: Int,
  fuel: Int,
) -> Closure / {abort.raise} =
  if stack_size <= 0 { { seen: seen, stack: stack, out: out, asked_looks: needs, sealed: false } }
  else if fuel <= 0 {
    panic(
      "the search visited the same step of the compiled pattern twice while computing one matcher state, but it must visit each step at most once",
    )
  } else {
    let pc = stack.get(stack_size - 1);
    if seen.get(pc) == stamp {
      epsilon_closure(
        instructions,
        have,
        cut,
        stamp,
        seen,
        stack,
        stack_size - 1,
        out,
        needs,
        fuel - 1,
      )
    } else {
      let marked = seen.set(pc, stamp);
      match instructions.get(pc) {
        Split(x, y) ->
          epsilon_closure(
            instructions,
            have,
            cut,
            stamp,
            marked,
            stack.set(stack_size - 1, y).set(stack_size, x),
            stack_size + 1,
            out,
            needs,
            fuel - 1,
          ),
        Save(_, to) ->
          epsilon_closure(
            instructions,
            have,
            cut,
            stamp,
            marked,
            stack.set(stack_size - 1, to),
            stack_size,
            out,
            needs,
            fuel - 1,
          ),
        Check(looks, to) -> if looks & ~have == 0 {
          epsilon_closure(
            instructions,
            have,
            cut,
            stamp,
            marked,
            stack.set(stack_size - 1, to),
            stack_size,
            out.push(pc),
            needs | looks,
            fuel - 1,
          )
        } else {
          epsilon_closure(
            instructions,
            have,
            cut,
            stamp,
            marked,
            stack,
            stack_size - 1,
            out.push(pc),
            needs | looks,
            fuel - 1,
          )
        },
        Fail ->
          epsilon_closure(
            instructions,
            have,
            cut,
            stamp,
            marked,
            stack,
            stack_size - 1,
            out,
            needs,
            fuel - 1,
          ),
        Match -> if cut {
          { seen: marked, stack: stack, out: out.push(pc), asked_looks: needs, sealed: true }
        } else {
          epsilon_closure(
            instructions,
            have,
            cut,
            stamp,
            marked,
            stack,
            stack_size - 1,
            out.push(pc),
            needs,
            fuel - 1,
          )
        },
        _ ->
          epsilon_closure(
            instructions,
            have,
            cut,
            stamp,
            marked,
            stack,
            stack_size - 1,
            out.push(pc),
            needs,
            fuel - 1,
          ),
      }
    }
  }

fn reclose(
  a: Automaton,
  key: List<Int>,
  i: Int,
  have: Int,
  stamp: Int,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  out: List<Int>,
  needs: Int,
) -> Closure / {abort.raise} =
  match key.at(i) {
    None -> { seen: seen, stack: stack, out: out, asked_looks: needs, sealed: false },
    Some(pc) -> {
      let c = epsilon_closure(
        a.instructions,
        have,
        false,
        stamp,
        seen,
        stack.set(0, pc),
        1,
        out,
        needs,
        4 * a.instructions.len() + 4,
      );
      reclose(a, key, i + 1, have, stamp, c.seen, c.stack, c.out, c.asked_looks)
    },
  }

type AdvanceResult = {
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  out: List<Int>,
  needs: Int,
  matched: Bool,
}

fn advance(
  a: Automaton,
  places: List<Int>,
  i: Int,
  b: Int,
  after: Int,
  stamp: Int,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  out: List<Int>,
  needs: Int,
  matched: Bool,
) -> AdvanceResult / {abort.raise} =
  match places.at(i) {
    None -> { seen: seen, stack: stack, out: out, needs: needs, matched: matched },
    Some(pc) -> {
      let to = match a.instructions.get(pc) {
        Range(lo, hi, to) -> if b >= lo && b <= hi { to } else { -1 },
        Switch(table, arms) -> {
          let arm = if b < 256 { table.at(b) } else { 0 };
          if arm > 0 { arms.get(arm - 1) } else { -1 }
        },
        Match -> -2,
        _ -> -1,
      };
      if to == -2 {
        if a.first_wins { { seen: seen, stack: stack, out: out, needs: needs, matched: true } }
        else { advance(a, places, i + 1, b, after, stamp, seen, stack, out, needs, true) }
      } else if to < 0 {
        advance(a, places, i + 1, b, after, stamp, seen, stack, out, needs, matched)
      } else {
        let c = epsilon_closure(
          a.instructions,
          after,
          a.first_wins,
          stamp,
          seen,
          stack.set(0, to),
          1,
          out,
          needs,
          4 * a.instructions.len() + 4,
        );
        if c.sealed {
          { seen: c.seen, stack: c.stack, out: c.out, needs: c.asked_looks, matched: matched }
        } else {
          advance(a, places, i + 1, b, after, stamp, c.seen, c.stack, c.out, c.asked_looks, matched)
        }
      }
    },
  }

type StateLookup = { states: States, to: Int }

fn state_of(a: Automaton, s: States, flags: Int, needs: Int, places: List<Int>) -> StateLookup =
  if places.len() == 0 { { states: s, to: 2 } } else {
    let key = List::fold(
      if a.first_wins { places } else { places.sort() },
      [if needs == 0 { 0 } else { flags }, needs],
      |k: List<Int>, pc: Int| k.push(pc),
    );
    match s.ids.get(key) {
      Some(id) -> { states: s, to: id * 2 },
      None -> if s.keys.len() >= s.room { { states: s, to: -1 } } else {
        let id = s.keys.len();
        { states: { ..s, ids: s.ids.insert(key, id), keys: s.keys.push(key) }, to: id * 2 }
      },
    }
  }

type TransitionResult = {
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  states: States,
  to: Int,
}

fn transition(
  a: Automaton,
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  s: States,
  stamp: Int,
  h: Int,
  b: Int,
) -> TransitionResult / {abort.raise} = {
  let key = match s.keys.at(h >> 1) {
    Some(k) -> k,
    None ->
      panic("this matcher state number was not created by this search, so it has no recorded key"),
  };
  let flags = key.at_or(0, 0);
  let needs = key.at_or(1, 0);
  let word = b < 256 && is_word(b);
  let before = flags & 63 | (if b == 10 { 2 } else if b == 256 { 10 } else { 0 })
    | (if word == (flags & 64 != 0) { 32 } else { 16 });
  let after = if b == 10 && a.lines { 1 } else { 0 };
  let again = needs & before & ~flags != 0;
  let walked = if again { reclose(a, key, 2, before, stamp, seen, stack, [], 0) }
  else { { seen: seen, stack: stack, out: key, asked_looks: 0, sealed: false } };
  let relocate = advance(
    a,
    walked.out,
    if again { 0 } else { 2 },
    b,
    after,
    stamp + 1,
    walked.seen,
    walked.stack,
    [],
    0,
    false,
  );
  let bit = if relocate.matched { 1 } else { 0 };
  let made = if b == 256 { { states: s, to: 2 } } else {
    state_of(a, s, after | (if word && a.words { 64 } else { 0 }), relocate.needs, relocate.out)
  };
  if made.to < 0 {
    { table: table, seen: relocate.seen, stack: relocate.stack, states: made.states, to: -1 }
  } else {
    let class = if b == 256 { a.stride - 1 } else { a.classes.at(b) };
    {
      table: table.set(s.base + (h >> 1) * a.stride + class, made.to | bit),
      seen: relocate.seen,
      stack: relocate.stack,
      states: made.states,
      to: made.to | bit,
    }
  }
}

type StartResult = { seen: Array<Int>, stack: Array<Int>, states: States, to: Int }

fn start_state(
  a: Automaton,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  s: States,
  stamp: Int,
  hay: Bytes,
  at: Int,
  backwards: Bool,
) -> StartResult / {abort.raise} = {
  let before = if backwards { if at < hay.len() { hay.at(at) } else { -1 } }
  else if at > 0 { hay.at(at - 1) }
  else { -1 };
  let kind = if before < 0 { 0 }
  else if before == 10 && a.lines { 1 }
  else if a.words && is_word(before) { 2 }
  else { 3 };
  let known = s.starts.at_or(kind, -1);
  if known >= 0 { { seen: seen, stack: stack, states: s, to: known } } else {
    let have = match kind { 0 -> 5, 1 -> 1, _ -> 0 };
    let walked = epsilon_closure(
      a.instructions,
      have,
      a.first_wins,
      stamp,
      seen,
      stack.set(0, a.entry),
      1,
      [],
      0,
      4 * a.instructions.len() + 4,
    );
    let made = state_of(
      a,
      s,
      have | (if kind == 2 { 64 } else { 0 }),
      walked.asked_looks,
      walked.out,
    );
    {
      seen: walked.seen,
      stack: walked.stack,
      states: if made.to < 0 { made.states }
      else { { ..made.states, starts: made.states.starts.set(kind, made.to) } },
      to: made.to,
    }
  }
}

type Scan = { at: Int, state: Int, last: Int, hit: Int }

fn scan_forward(
  table: Array<Int>,
  classes: Bytes,
  hay: Bytes,
  stride: Int,
  base: Int,
  i: Int,
  stop: Int,
  h: Int,
  last: Int,
  quick: Bool,
  home: Int,
  first: Bytes,
  lead: Bytes,
  left: Int,
) -> Scan / {abort.raise} =
  if i >= stop { { at: i, state: h, last: last, hit: 1 } }
  else if left <= 0 { panic("a scan reads each byte once") } else {
    let j = if h != home { i } else if lead.len() > 1 {
      match hay.index_of_from(lead, i) { Some(found) -> found, None -> stop }
    } else { hay.scan_until(i, first, stop - i) };
    if j >= stop { { at: stop, state: h, last: last, hit: 1 } } else {
      let to = table.get(base + (h >> 1) * stride + classes.at(hay.at(j)));
      if to < 4 { { at: j, state: h, last: last, hit: to } } else if to & 1 == 0 {
        scan_forward(
          table,
          classes,
          hay,
          stride,
          base,
          j + 1,
          stop,
          to,
          last,
          quick,
          home,
          first,
          lead,
          left - 1,
        )
      } else if quick { { at: j, state: to, last: j, hit: 3 } } else {
        scan_forward(
          table,
          classes,
          hay,
          stride,
          base,
          j + 1,
          stop,
          to,
          j,
          quick,
          home,
          first,
          lead,
          left - 1,
        )
      }
    }
  }

fn scan_reverse(
  table: Array<Int>,
  classes: Bytes,
  hay: Bytes,
  stride: Int,
  base: Int,
  i: Int,
  stop: Int,
  h: Int,
  last: Int,
) -> Scan / {abort.raise} =
  if i <= stop { { at: i, state: h, last: last, hit: 1 } } else {
    let to = table.get(base + (h >> 1) * stride + classes.at(hay.at(i - 1)));
    if to < 4 { { at: i, state: h, last: last, hit: to } } else {
      scan_reverse(table, classes, hay, stride, base, i - 1, stop, to, if to & 1 == 1 { i }
      else { last })
    }
  }

type StateSearchResult = {
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  states: States,
  stamp: Int,
  at: Int,
}

fn search_forward(
  a: Automaton,
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  s: States,
  stamp: Int,
  hay: Bytes,
  i: Int,
  h: Int,
  last: Int,
  quick: Bool,
  home: Int,
  o: Prefilter,
  left: Int,
) -> StateSearchResult / {abort.raise} = {
  let n = hay.len();
  let read = scan_forward(
    table,
    a.classes,
    hay,
    a.stride,
    s.base,
    i,
    n,
    h,
    last,
    quick,
    home,
    o.first,
    o.prefix,
    n - i + 1,
  );
  match read.hit {
    2 -> { table: table, seen: seen, stack: stack, states: s, stamp: stamp, at: read.last },
    3 -> { table: table, seen: seen, stack: stack, states: s, stamp: stamp, at: read.at },
    1 -> {
      let known = table.get(s.base + (read.state >> 1) * a.stride + a.stride - 1);
      if known != 0 {
        {
          table: table,
          seen: seen,
          stack: stack,
          states: s,
          stamp: stamp,
          at: if known & 1 == 1 { n } else { read.last },
        }
      } else {
        let ended = transition(a, table, seen, stack, s, stamp, read.state, 256);
        {
          table: ended.table,
          seen: ended.seen,
          stack: ended.stack,
          states: ended.states,
          stamp: stamp + 2,
          at: if ended.to & 1 == 1 { n } else { read.last },
        }
      }
    },
    _ -> if left <= 0 { panic("a search makes a state for each byte at most") } else {
      let made = transition(a, table, seen, stack, s, stamp, read.state, hay.at(read.at));
      if made.to < 0 {
        {
          table: made.table,
          seen: made.seen,
          stack: made.stack,
          states: made.states,
          stamp: stamp + 2,
          at: -2,
        }
      } else {
        search_forward(
          a,
          made.table,
          made.seen,
          made.stack,
          made.states,
          stamp + 2,
          hay,
          read.at,
          read.state,
          read.last,
          quick,
          home,
          o,
          left - 1,
        )
      }
    },
  }
}

fn search_reverse(
  a: Automaton,
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  s: States,
  stamp: Int,
  hay: Bytes,
  i: Int,
  stop: Int,
  h: Int,
  last: Int,
  left: Int,
) -> StateSearchResult / {abort.raise} = {
  let read = scan_reverse(table, a.classes, hay, a.stride, s.base, i, stop, h, last);
  match read.hit {
    2 -> { table: table, seen: seen, stack: stack, states: s, stamp: stamp, at: read.last },
    3 -> { table: table, seen: seen, stack: stack, states: s, stamp: stamp, at: read.at },
    1 -> {
      let b = if stop > 0 { hay.at(stop - 1) } else { 256 };
      let class = if b == 256 { a.stride - 1 } else { a.classes.at(b) };
      let known = table.get(s.base + (read.state >> 1) * a.stride + class);
      if known != 0 {
        {
          table: table,
          seen: seen,
          stack: stack,
          states: s,
          stamp: stamp,
          at: if known & 1 == 1 { stop } else { read.last },
        }
      } else {
        let ended = transition(a, table, seen, stack, s, stamp, read.state, b);
        {
          table: ended.table,
          seen: ended.seen,
          stack: ended.stack,
          states: ended.states,
          stamp: stamp + 2,
          at: if ended.to < 0 { -2 } else if ended.to & 1 == 1 { stop } else { read.last },
        }
      }
    },
    _ -> if left <= 0 { panic("a search makes a state for each byte at most") } else {
      let made = transition(a, table, seen, stack, s, stamp, read.state, hay.at(read.at - 1));
      if made.to < 0 {
        {
          table: made.table,
          seen: made.seen,
          stack: made.stack,
          states: made.states,
          stamp: stamp + 2,
          at: -2,
        }
      } else {
        search_reverse(
          a,
          made.table,
          made.seen,
          made.stack,
          made.states,
          stamp + 2,
          hay,
          read.at,
          stop,
          read.state,
          read.last,
          left - 1,
        )
      }
    },
  }
}

type Hit = {
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  explored: SearchCache,
  slots: Array<Int>,
}

fn search(
  re: Compiled,
  hay: Bytes,
  from: Int,
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  explored: SearchCache,
  want: Int,
) -> Hit / {abort.raise} =
  if re.prefilter.exact {
    let found = if re.prefilter.prefix.len() == 0 { Some(from) }
    else { hay.index_of_from(re.prefilter.prefix, from) };
    match found {
      Some(at) ->
        capture_known_match(
          re,
          hay,
          at,
          at + re.prefilter.prefix.len(),
          table,
          seen,
          stack,
          explored,
          want,
        ),
      None ->
        { table: table, seen: seen, stack: stack, explored: explored, slots: Array::of_list([]) },
    }
  } else if lacks_required(re, hay, from) {
    { table: table, seen: seen, stack: stack, explored: explored, slots: Array::of_list([]) }
  } else if explored.overflowed || re.wide || re.options.state_limit <= 0
      || hay.len() - from <= re.options.short {
    by_threads(re, hay, from, table, seen, stack, explored, want)
  } else if table.len() > 0 { by_states(re, hay, from, table, seen, stack, explored, want) } else {
    let rows = state_capacity(re, hay) + 2;
    let most = max(re.finder.instructions.len(), re.reverse.instructions.len());
    by_states(
      re,
      hay,
      from,
      Array::new((if re.options.longest { 3 } else { 2 }) * rows * re.finder.stride, 0),
      Array::new(most, 0),
      Array::new(2 * most + 2, 0),
      {
        stamp: 1,
        ahead: empty_states(rows - 2, 0),
        back: empty_states(rows - 2, rows * re.finder.stride),
        stretch: empty_states(rows - 2, 2 * rows * re.finder.stride),
        overflowed: false,
      },
      want,
    )
  }

fn state_capacity(re: Compiled, hay: Bytes) -> Int / {abort.raise} =
  min(min(re.options.state_limit, hay.len() + 2), 0x4000000 / (3 * re.finder.stride) - 2)

fn lacks_required(re: Compiled, hay: Bytes, from: Int) -> Bool / {abort.raise} =
  re.prefilter.required.len() > 0 && hay.index_of_from(re.prefilter.required, from) == None

fn by_threads(
  re: Compiled,
  hay: Bytes,
  from: Int,
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  explored: SearchCache,
  want: Int,
) -> Hit / {abort.raise} =
  {
    table: table,
    seen: seen,
    stack: stack,
    explored: explored,
    slots: run(
      {
        instructions: re.instructions,
        hay: hay,
        stop: hay.len(),
        slots: want,
        longest: re.options.longest,
        wide: re.wide,
      },
      re.search,
      from,
    ),
  }

fn capture_known_match(
  re: Compiled,
  hay: Bytes,
  start: Int,
  end: Int,
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  explored: SearchCache,
  want: Int,
) -> Hit / {abort.raise} =
  {
    table: table,
    seen: seen,
    stack: stack,
    explored: explored,
    slots: if want <= 2 || re.names.len() == 1 { Array::of_list([start, end]) } else {
      run(
        {
          instructions: re.instructions,
          hay: hay,
          stop: end,
          slots: want,
          longest: re.options.longest,
          wide: re.wide,
        },
        re.start,
        start,
      )
    },
  }

fn by_states(
  re: Compiled,
  hay: Bytes,
  from: Int,
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  explored: SearchCache,
  want: Int,
) -> Hit / {abort.raise} = {
  let first = start_state(re.finder, seen, stack, explored.ahead, explored.stamp, hay, from, false);
  if first.to < 0 {
    by_threads(
      re,
      hay,
      from,
      table,
      first.seen,
      first.stack,
      { ..explored, stamp: explored.stamp + 1, overflowed: true },
      want,
    )
  } else {
    let home = if re.prefilter.prefix.len() > 1 || re.prefilter.first.len() > 0 { first.to }
    else { -1 };
    let end = search_forward(
      re.finder,
      table,
      first.seen,
      first.stack,
      first.states,
      explored.stamp + 1,
      hay,
      from,
      first.to,
      -1,
      false,
      home,
      re.prefilter,
      hay.len() - from + 3,
    );
    let updated_cache = { ..explored, stamp: end.stamp, ahead: end.states };
    if end.at == -2 {
      by_threads(
        re,
        hay,
        from,
        end.table,
        end.seen,
        end.stack,
        { ..updated_cache, overflowed: true },
        want,
      )
    } else if end.at < 0 {
      {
        table: end.table,
        seen: end.seen,
        stack: end.stack,
        explored: updated_cache,
        slots: Array::of_list([]),
      }
    } else {
      find_start(re, hay, from, end.at, end.table, end.seen, end.stack, updated_cache, want)
    }
  }
}

fn find_start(
  re: Compiled,
  hay: Bytes,
  from: Int,
  end: Int,
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  explored: SearchCache,
  want: Int,
) -> Hit / {abort.raise} = {
  let first = start_state(re.reverse, seen, stack, explored.back, explored.stamp, hay, end, true);
  if first.to < 0 {
    by_threads(
      re,
      hay,
      from,
      table,
      first.seen,
      first.stack,
      { ..explored, stamp: explored.stamp + 1, overflowed: true },
      want,
    )
  } else {
    let start = search_reverse(
      re.reverse,
      table,
      first.seen,
      first.stack,
      first.states,
      explored.stamp + 1,
      hay,
      end,
      from,
      first.to,
      -1,
      end - from + 3,
    );
    let updated_cache = { ..explored, stamp: start.stamp, back: start.states };
    if start.at == -2 {
      by_threads(
        re,
        hay,
        from,
        start.table,
        start.seen,
        start.stack,
        { ..updated_cache, overflowed: true },
        want,
      )
    } else if start.at < 0 {
      panic("searching backwards from the end of a match must find its start")
    } else if re.options.longest {
      find_longest_end(re, hay, start.at, start.table, start.seen, start.stack, updated_cache, want)
    } else {
      capture_known_match(
        re,
        hay,
        start.at,
        end,
        start.table,
        start.seen,
        start.stack,
        updated_cache,
        want,
      )
    }
  }
}

fn find_longest_end(
  re: Compiled,
  hay: Bytes,
  start: Int,
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  explored: SearchCache,
  want: Int,
) -> Hit / {abort.raise} = {
  let first = start_state(
    re.longest_finder,
    seen,
    stack,
    explored.stretch,
    explored.stamp,
    hay,
    start,
    false,
  );
  if first.to < 0 {
    by_threads(
      re,
      hay,
      start,
      table,
      first.seen,
      first.stack,
      { ..explored, stamp: explored.stamp + 1, overflowed: true },
      want,
    )
  } else {
    let end = search_forward(
      re.longest_finder,
      table,
      first.seen,
      first.stack,
      first.states,
      explored.stamp + 1,
      hay,
      start,
      first.to,
      -1,
      false,
      -1,
      re.prefilter,
      hay.len() - start + 3,
    );
    let updated_cache = { ..explored, stamp: end.stamp, stretch: end.states };
    if end.at == -2 {
      by_threads(
        re,
        hay,
        start,
        end.table,
        end.seen,
        end.stack,
        { ..updated_cache, overflowed: true },
        want,
      )
    } else if end.at < 0 { panic("searching forwards from the start of a match must find its end") }
    else {
      capture_known_match(
        re,
        hay,
        start,
        end.at,
        end.table,
        end.seen,
        end.stack,
        updated_cache,
        want,
      )
    }
  }
}

fn has_match(re: Compiled, hay: Bytes) -> Bool / {abort.raise} =
  if re.prefilter.exact {
    re.prefilter.prefix.len() == 0 || hay.index_of(re.prefilter.prefix) != None
  } else { !lacks_required(re, hay, 0) && has_match_by_states(re, hay) }

fn has_match_by_states(re: Compiled, hay: Bytes) -> Bool / {abort.raise} =
  if re.wide || re.options.state_limit <= 0 || hay.len() <= re.options.short {
    has_match_by_threads(re, hay)
  } else {
    let a = re.finder;
    let room = state_capacity(re, hay);
    let first = start_state(
      a,
      Array::new(a.instructions.len(), 0),
      Array::new(2 * a.instructions.len() + 2, 0),
      empty_states(room, 0),
      1,
      hay,
      0,
      false,
    );
    if first.to < 0 { has_match_by_threads(re, hay) } else {
      let home = if re.prefilter.prefix.len() > 1 || re.prefilter.first.len() > 0 { first.to }
      else { -1 };
      let end = search_forward(
        a,
        Array::new((room + 2) * a.stride, 0),
        first.seen,
        first.stack,
        first.states,
        2,
        hay,
        0,
        first.to,
        -1,
        true,
        home,
        re.prefilter,
        hay.len() + 3,
      );
      if end.at == -2 { has_match_by_threads(re, hay) } else { end.at >= 0 }
    }
  }

fn has_match_by_threads(re: Compiled, hay: Bytes) -> Bool / {abort.raise} =
  run(
      {
        instructions: re.instructions,
        hay: hay,
        stop: hay.len(),
        slots: 2,
        longest: false,
        wide: re.wide,
      },
      re.search,
      0,
    ).len(
    )
    > 0

fn next_char_start(re: Compiled, hay: Bytes, at: Int) -> Int / {abort.raise} =
  if re.matches_bytes || at >= hay.len() { at + 1 } else {
    let lead = hay.at(at);
    if lead < 0x80 { at + 1 }
    else if lead < 0xE0 { at + 2 }
    else if lead < 0xF0 { at + 3 }
    else { at + 4 }
  }

fn matches(re: Compiled, hay: Bytes, want: Int, most: Int) -> List<Array<Int>> / {abort.raise} =
  matches_from(
    re,
    hay,
    want,
    most,
    0,
    -1,
    Array::of_list([]),
    Array::of_list([]),
    Array::of_list([]),
    empty_search_cache,
    [],
    hay.len() + 2,
  )

fn matches_from(
  re: Compiled,
  hay: Bytes,
  want: Int,
  most: Int,
  from: Int,
  ended: Int,
  table: Array<Int>,
  seen: Array<Int>,
  stack: Array<Int>,
  explored: SearchCache,
  found: List<Array<Int>>,
  left: Int,
) -> List<Array<Int>> / {abort.raise} =
  if from > hay.len() || found.len() == most || left <= 0 { found } else {
    let hit = search(re, hay, from, table, seen, stack, explored, want);
    if hit.slots.len() == 0 { found } else {
      let start = hit.slots.get(0);
      let end = hit.slots.get(1);
      if end == start && start == ended {
        matches_from(
          re,
          hay,
          want,
          most,
          next_char_start(re, hay, start),
          ended,
          hit.table,
          hit.seen,
          hit.stack,
          hit.explored,
          found,
          left - 1,
        )
      } else {
        matches_from(
          re,
          hay,
          want,
          most,
          if end == start { next_char_start(re, hay, end) } else { end },
          end,
          hit.table,
          hit.seen,
          hit.stack,
          hit.explored,
          found.push(hit.slots),
          left - 1,
        )
      }
    }
  }

/// A pattern compiled to search a `String` one character at a time. Two are equal when their
/// pattern text and options are equal, and its printed form is its pattern.
pub type Regex = | Regex(Compiled)

key for Regex by equality_key

show for Regex by pattern

fn equality_key(re: Regex) -> { pattern: String, options: Options } =
  match re { Regex(c) -> { pattern: c.pattern, options: c.options } }

/// The pattern `re` was compiled from, as it was written.
pub fn pattern(re: Regex) -> String = match re { Regex(c) -> c.pattern }

fn inner(re: Regex) -> Compiled = match re { Regex(c) -> c }

/// Where a match, or a group of one, lies in its subject: from `start` up to `end`, counted in
/// characters of a `String` and in bytes of a `Bytes`, as `String::slice` and `Bytes::slice`
/// count them.
pub type Span = { start: Int, end: Int }

/// The groups captured by one match: each group's span by group number, with the whole match as
/// group 0, and `None` for a group that did not take part in the match.
pub type Captures = new { groups: List<Option<Span>>, numbers: Map<String, Int> }

/// The pattern compiled under `options()`, or where and why it is rejected.
pub fn compile(pattern: String) -> Result<Regex, Error> / {abort.raise} =
  try { read(pattern, options) }

/// The pattern compiled as `o` says, or where and why it is rejected.
pub fn compile_with(pattern: String, o: Options) -> Result<Regex, Error> / {abort.raise} =
  try { read(pattern, o) }

/// The pattern compiled as `o` says, raising `regex.fail` where `compile_with` returns `Err`.
pub fn read(pattern: String, o: Options) -> Regex / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  Regex(compiled(pattern, o, false))

/// Returns a canonical form of the pattern: every flag written out where it applies and every class
/// written as ranges. Compiling it gives a program equivalent to `re`.
pub fn normalized_pattern(re: Regex) -> String / {abort.raise} = node_text(inner(re).tree, 0, false)

/// How many groups the pattern has, the whole match counted as one.
pub fn group_count(re: Regex) -> Int = inner(re).names.len()

/// Each group's name by its number, `None` for one with none, as the whole match has none.
pub fn group_names(re: Regex) -> List<Option<String>> = inner(re).names

/// Whether a match stands anywhere in `text`.
pub fn is_match(re: Regex, text: String) -> Bool / {abort.raise} =
  has_match(inner(re), Bytes::of_string(text))

/// The leftmost match in `text`.
pub fn find(re: Regex, text: String) -> Option<Span> / {abort.raise} =
  match char_spans(text, matches(inner(re), Bytes::of_string(text), 2, 1)).at(0) {
    Some([Some(span), ..]) -> Some(span),
    _ -> None,
  }

/// Every match in `text`, in order and none overlapping another. A search starts where the
/// last match ended, and one character on from an empty one; an empty match is passed over where
/// the match before it ended.
pub fn find_all(re: Regex, text: String) -> List<Span> / {abort.raise} =
  char_spans(text, matches(inner(re), Bytes::of_string(text), 2, -1)).fold(
    [],
    |spans: List<Span>, groups: List<Option<Span>>|
      match groups { [Some(span), ..] -> spans.push(span), _ -> spans },
  )

/// The leftmost match in `text`, with what each group captured.
pub fn captures(re: Regex, text: String) -> Option<Captures> / {abort.raise} =
  captures_all_of(re, text, 1).at(0)

/// Every match in `text`, as `find_all` finds them, each with what its groups captured.
pub fn captures_all(re: Regex, text: String) -> List<Captures> / {abort.raise} =
  captures_all_of(re, text, -1)

fn captures_all_of(re: Regex, text: String, most: Int) -> List<Captures> / {abort.raise} = {
  let c = inner(re);
  char_spans(text, matches(c, Bytes::of_string(text), 2 * c.names.len(), most)).map(
    |groups: List<Option<Span>>| -> Captures { { groups: groups, numbers: c.numbers } },
  )
}

/// Returns the span of the group numbered `index`, or `None` when the group did not take part in
/// the match or the pattern has no such group.
pub fn group(c: Captures, index: Int) -> Option<Span> =
  match c.groups.at(index) { Some(span) -> span, None -> None }

/// Returns the span of the group named `name`, or `None` when the group did not take part in the
/// match or the pattern has no such group.
pub fn named(c: Captures, name: String) -> Option<Span> =
  match c.numbers.get(name) { Some(index) -> group(c, index), None -> None }

/// The part of `text` a span of it covers.
pub fn slice(text: String, span: Span) -> String / {abort.raise} = text.slice(span.start, span.end)

fn char_spans(text: String, found: List<Array<Int>>) -> List<List<Option<Span>>> / {abort.raise} = {
  let hay = Bytes::of_string(text);
  let plain = hay.len() == text.len();
  found.fold(
    { byte: 0, char: 0, all: [] },
    |rewrite_case: { byte: Int, char: Int, all: List<List<Option<Span>>> }, slots: Array<Int>| {
      let start = if plain { slots.get(0) }
      else { rewrite_case.char + chars_in(hay, rewrite_case.byte, slots.get(0)) };
      let groups = range(0, slots.len() / 2).map(|g: Int| {
        let from = slots.get(2 * g);
        let to = slots.get(2 * g + 1);
        if from < 0 || to < 0 { None }
        else if plain { Some({ start: from, end: to }) } else {
          let first = start + chars_in(hay, slots.get(0), from);
          Some({ start: first, end: first + chars_in(hay, from, to) })
        }
      });
      {
        byte: slots.get(1),
        char: if plain { 0 } else { start + chars_in(hay, slots.get(0), slots.get(1)) },
        all: rewrite_case.all.push(groups),
      }
    },
  ).all
}

fn chars_in(hay: Bytes, from: Int, to: Int) -> Int / {abort.raise} =
  String::of_bytes(hay.slice(from, to)).len()

type Part = | Verbatim(String) | Group(Int)

/// A replacement text parsed into parts. `$1` or `${1}` inserts the group with that number, `$name`
/// or `${name}` inserts the group with that name (the name extends over letters, digits and `_`),
/// and `$$` inserts a `$`. A group that did not take part in the match inserts nothing.
pub type Template = new { parts: List<Part> }

/// Parses `text` as a replacement template for matches of `re`. Returns `Err` with the position and
/// reason when a `$` is not followed by a valid group reference or another `$`, or when a
/// referenced group does not exist in `re`.
pub fn template(re: Regex, text: String) -> Result<Template, Error> / {abort.raise} =
  try { read_template(re, text) }

/// As `template`, raising `regex.fail` where that returns `Err`.
pub fn read_template(re: Regex, text: String) -> Template / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  parse_template(inner(re), text)

fn parse_template(re: Compiled, text: String) -> Template / {regex.fail, abort.raise} = {
  let code_points = Array::of_list(text.code_points());
  { parts: template_parts(re, text, code_points, 0, 0, [], code_points.len() + 1) }
}

fn template_parts(
  re: Compiled,
  text: String,
  code_points: Array<Int>,
  from: Int,
  at: Int,
  parts: List<Part>,
  left: Int,
) -> List<Part> / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  if left <= 0 {
    panic("the parser cannot finish: it found more parts than there are characters left to read")
  } else {
    match code_points.at(at) {
      None -> verbatim(text, from, at, parts),
      Some(c) -> if c != b'$' {
        template_parts(re, text, code_points, from, at + 1, parts, left - 1)
      } else {
        let before = verbatim(text, from, at, parts);
        let next = match code_points.at(at + 1) { Some(n) -> n, None -> -1 };
        if next == b'$' {
          template_parts(
            re,
            text,
            code_points,
            at + 2,
            at + 2,
            before.push(Verbatim("$")),
            left - 1,
          )
        } else {
          let braced = meta(next) == Brace;
          let open = if braced { at + 2 } else { at + 1 };
          let end = name_end(code_points, open);
          if braced && code_points.at(end) != Some(b'}') { fail(at, UnclosedName) }
          else if end == open { fail(at, if braced { NoSuchGroup } else { LoneDollar }) } else {
            let after = if braced { end + 1 } else { end };
            template_parts(
              re,
              text,
              code_points,
              after,
              after,
              before.push(Group(group_index(re, name_text(code_points, open, end), at))),
              left - 1,
            )
          }
        }
      },
    }
  }

fn verbatim(text: String, from: Int, to: Int, parts: List<Part>) -> List<Part> / {abort.raise} =
  if to > from { parts.push(Verbatim(text.slice(from, to))) } else { parts }

fn group_index(re: Compiled, name: String, at: Int) -> Int / {regex.fail} = {
  let digits = Bytes::of_string(name);
  let number = if digits.scan(0, b"0123456789", digits.len()) < digits.len() {
    re.numbers.get(name)
  } else {
    Some(
      range(0, digits.len()).fold(0, |n: Int, i: Int|
        if n > 100000 { n } else { n * 10 + digits.at(i) - 48 }),
    )
  };
  match number { Some(index) if index < re.names.len() -> index, _ -> fail(at, NoSuchGroup) }
}

fn uses_groups(t: Template) -> Bool =
  t.parts.fold(false, |any: Bool, p: Part|
    any || (match p { Group(index) -> index > 0, Verbatim(_) -> false }))

fn expand_template(t: Template, hay: Bytes, slots: Array<Int>) -> Bytes / {abort.raise} =
  Bytes::concat_all(
    t.parts.map(|p: Part|
      match p {
        Verbatim(text) -> Bytes::of_string(text),
        Group(index) -> {
          let from = match slots.at(2 * index) { Some(at) -> at, None -> -1 };
          let to = match slots.at(2 * index + 1) { Some(at) -> at, None -> -1 };
          if from < 0 || to < 0 { b"" } else { hay.slice(from, to) }
        },
      }),
  )

fn replace_matches(re: Compiled, hay: Bytes, t: Template, most: Int) -> Bytes / {abort.raise} = {
  let want = if uses_groups(t) { 2 * re.names.len() } else { 2 };
  let rewrite_case = matches(re, hay, want, most).fold(
    { at: 0, parts: [] },
    |rewrite_case: { at: Int, parts: List<Bytes> }, slots: Array<Int>|
      {
        at: slots.get(1),
        parts: rewrite_case.parts.push(hay.slice(rewrite_case.at, slots.get(0))).push(
          expand_template(t, hay, slots),
        ),
      },
  );
  Bytes::concat_all(rewrite_case.parts.push(hay.slice(rewrite_case.at, hay.len())))
}

/// `text` with its leftmost match replaced by what the template writes for it.
pub fn replace(re: Regex, text: String, to: Template) -> String / {abort.raise} =
  String::of_bytes(replace_matches(inner(re), Bytes::of_string(text), to, 1))

/// `text` with every match, as `find_all` finds them, replaced by what the template writes
/// for it.
pub fn replace_all(re: Regex, text: String, to: Template) -> String / {abort.raise} =
  String::of_bytes(replace_matches(inner(re), Bytes::of_string(text), to, -1))

/// `text` with its leftmost match replaced by what `each` returns for what it captured.
pub fn replace_with<| e>(
  re: Regex,
  text: String,
  each: (Captures) -> String / e,
) -> String / {abort.raise | e} = replace_matches_with(re, text, each, 1)

/// Returns `text` with every match, found as `find_all` finds them, replaced by the string that
/// `each` returns for that match's captures.
pub fn replace_all_with<| e>(
  re: Regex,
  text: String,
  each: (Captures) -> String / e,
) -> String / {abort.raise | e} = replace_matches_with(re, text, each, -1)

fn replace_matches_with<| e>(
  re: Regex,
  text: String,
  each: (Captures) -> String / e,
  most: Int,
) -> String / {abort.raise | e} = {
  let rewrite_case = captures_all_of(re, text, most).fold(
    { at: 0, parts: [] },
    |rewrite_case: { at: Int, parts: List<String> }, c: Captures|
      match group(c, 0) {
        Some(whole) ->
          {
            at: whole.end,
            parts: rewrite_case.parts.push(text.slice(rewrite_case.at, whole.start)).push(each(c)),
          },
        None -> rewrite_case,
      },
  );
  String::join(rewrite_case.parts.push(text.slice(rewrite_case.at, text.len())), "")
}

fn split_matches(re: Compiled, hay: Bytes, most: Int) -> List<Bytes> / {abort.raise} = {
  let rewrite_case = matches(re, hay, 2, most).fold(
    { at: 0, parts: [] },
    |rewrite_case: { at: Int, parts: List<Bytes> }, slots: Array<Int>|
      {
        at: slots.get(1),
        parts: rewrite_case.parts.push(hay.slice(rewrite_case.at, slots.get(0))),
      },
  );
  rewrite_case.parts.push(hay.slice(rewrite_case.at, hay.len()))
}

/// Returns the pieces of `text` between its matches, found as `find_all` finds them. There is one
/// more piece than there are matches, so putting the matched text back between the pieces gives
/// `text`.
pub fn split(re: Regex, text: String) -> List<String> / {abort.raise} =
  split_matches(inner(re), Bytes::of_string(text), -1).map(|part: Bytes| String::of_bytes(part))

/// Returns at most `limit` pieces of `text`. Each piece but the last lies between two matches; the
/// last is all the text after the final match used. Returns no pieces where `limit` is not
/// positive.
pub fn splitn(re: Regex, text: String, limit: Int) -> List<String> / {abort.raise} =
  if limit <= 0 { [] } else {
    split_matches(inner(re), Bytes::of_string(text), limit - 1).map(|part: Bytes|
      String::of_bytes(part))
  }

/// Returns a pattern that matches `text` literally, by putting a `\` before each character that has
/// a special meaning in patterns.
pub fn escape(text: String) -> String =
  String::of_chars(
    text.chars().fold([], |accumulator: List<Char>, c: Char|
      if special(Int::of_char(c)) { accumulator.push('\\').push(c) } else { accumulator.push(c) }),
  )

fn special(c: Int) -> Bool = meta(c) != Plain || c == b']' || c == b'}'

/// A pattern compiled to search `Bytes` one byte at a time. A character in the pattern stands for
/// the byte with that number, so `\xFF` and `[\x80-\xFF]` match bytes, `.` matches any byte except
/// a line feed, and a character above `U+00FF` is rejected. Two `ByteRegex` values are equal when
/// they have the same pattern text and the same options. Showing one gives its pattern text.
pub type ByteRegex = | ByteRegex(Compiled)

key for ByteRegex by byte_equality_key

show for ByteRegex by byte_pattern

fn byte_equality_key(re: ByteRegex) -> { pattern: String, options: Options } =
  match re { ByteRegex(c) -> { pattern: c.pattern, options: c.options } }

/// The pattern `re` was compiled from, as it was written.
pub fn byte_pattern(re: ByteRegex) -> String = match re { ByteRegex(c) -> c.pattern }

fn byte_inner(re: ByteRegex) -> Compiled = match re { ByteRegex(c) -> c }

/// The pattern compiled over bytes under `options()`, or where and why it is rejected.
pub fn compile_bytes(pattern: String) -> Result<ByteRegex, Error> / {abort.raise} =
  try { read_bytes(pattern, options) }

/// The pattern compiled over bytes as `o` says, or where and why it is rejected.
pub fn compile_bytes_with(pattern: String, o: Options) -> Result<ByteRegex, Error> / {abort.raise} =
  try { read_bytes(pattern, o) }

/// The pattern compiled over bytes as `o` says, raising `regex.fail` where
/// `compile_bytes_with` returns `Err`.
pub fn read_bytes(pattern: String, o: Options) -> ByteRegex / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  ByteRegex(compiled(pattern, o, true))

/// Returns the pattern rewritten from its parsed form, as `normalized_pattern` does for text
/// patterns. A byte that is not valid text is written as `\x{NN}`.
pub fn normalized_byte_pattern(re: ByteRegex) -> String / {abort.raise} =
  node_text(byte_inner(re).tree, 0, true)

/// Whether a match stands anywhere in `hay`.
pub fn is_match_bytes(re: ByteRegex, hay: Bytes) -> Bool / {abort.raise} =
  has_match(byte_inner(re), hay)

/// The leftmost match in `hay`.
pub fn find_bytes(re: ByteRegex, hay: Bytes) -> Option<Span> / {abort.raise} =
  match matches(byte_inner(re), hay, 2, 1) {
    [slots] -> Some({ start: slots.get(0), end: slots.get(1) }),
    _ -> None,
  }

/// Returns every match in `hay`, in order and without overlaps, found as `find_all` finds them in
/// text but with byte offsets.
pub fn find_all_bytes(re: ByteRegex, hay: Bytes) -> List<Span> / {abort.raise} =
  matches(byte_inner(re), hay, 2, -1).map(|slots: Array<Int>|
    { start: slots.get(0), end: slots.get(1) })

/// The leftmost match in `hay`, with what each group captured.
pub fn captures_bytes(re: ByteRegex, hay: Bytes) -> Option<Captures> / {abort.raise} =
  byte_captures(byte_inner(re), hay, 1).at(0)

/// Every match in `hay`, as `find_all_bytes` finds them, each with what its groups captured.
pub fn captures_all_bytes(re: ByteRegex, hay: Bytes) -> List<Captures> / {abort.raise} =
  byte_captures(byte_inner(re), hay, -1)

fn byte_captures(re: Compiled, hay: Bytes, most: Int) -> List<Captures> / {abort.raise} =
  matches(re, hay, 2 * re.names.len(), most).map(|slots: Array<Int>| -> Captures {
    {
      groups: range(0, slots.len() / 2).map(|g: Int| {
        let from = slots.get(2 * g);
        let to = slots.get(2 * g + 1);
        if from < 0 || to < 0 { None } else { Some({ start: from, end: to }) }
      }),
      numbers: re.numbers,
    }
  })

/// Parses `text` as a replacement template for matches of `re`, as `template` does, and returns it
/// or where and why it is rejected. The template writes its literal text as UTF-8 bytes.
pub fn template_bytes(re: ByteRegex, text: String) -> Result<Template, Error> / {abort.raise} =
  try { read_template_bytes(re, text) }

/// As `template_bytes`, raising `regex.fail` where that returns `Err`.
pub fn read_template_bytes(re: ByteRegex, text: String) -> Template / {regex.fail, abort.raise} =
  parse_template(byte_inner(re), text)

/// `hay` with its leftmost match replaced by what the template writes for it.
pub fn replace_bytes(re: ByteRegex, hay: Bytes, to: Template) -> Bytes / {abort.raise} =
  replace_matches(byte_inner(re), hay, to, 1)

/// `hay` with every match, as `find_all_bytes` finds them, replaced by what the template writes
/// for it.
pub fn replace_all_bytes(re: ByteRegex, hay: Bytes, to: Template) -> Bytes / {abort.raise} =
  replace_matches(byte_inner(re), hay, to, -1)

/// The parts of `hay` between its matches, as `find_all_bytes` finds them: one more part than
/// there are matches.
pub fn split_bytes(re: ByteRegex, hay: Bytes) -> List<Bytes> / {abort.raise} =
  split_matches(byte_inner(re), hay, -1)

/// Returns at most `limit` pieces of `hay`, split as `splitn` splits text.
pub fn splitn_bytes(re: ByteRegex, hay: Bytes, limit: Int) -> List<Bytes> / {abort.raise} =
  if limit <= 0 { [] } else { split_matches(byte_inner(re), hay, limit - 1) }

fn must_with(pattern: String, o: Options) -> Regex / {abort.raise} =
  match compile_with(pattern, o) {
    Ok(re) -> re,
    Err(e) -> panic(f"`{pattern}` is rejected at {e.at}: {reason(e.reason)}"),
  }

fn must(pattern: String) -> Regex / {abort.raise} = must_with(pattern, options)

fn must_bytes(pattern: String) -> ByteRegex / {abort.raise} =
  match compile_bytes(pattern) {
    Ok(re) -> re,
    Err(e) -> panic(f"`{pattern}` is rejected at {e.at}: {reason(e.reason)}"),
  }

fn must_template(re: Regex, text: String) -> Template / {abort.raise} =
  match template(re, text) {
    Ok(t) -> t,
    Err(e) -> panic(f"`{text}` is rejected at {e.at}: {reason(e.reason)}"),
  }

const threads_only: Options = { ..options, state_limit: 0 }

const states_always: Options = { ..options, short: -1 }

const states_cramped: Options = { ..options, short: -1, state_limit: 3 }

type RewriteCase = { pattern: String, text: String }

fn rewrite_case(pattern: String, text: String) -> RewriteCase = { pattern: pattern, text: text }

const rewrites: List<RewriteCase> =
  [
    rewrite_case("abc", "abc"),
    rewrite_case("a|b|c", "a|b|c"),
    rewrite_case("a(?:b|c)d", "a(?:b|c)d"),
    rewrite_case("a|(?:b|c)", "a|b|c"),
    rewrite_case("a(?:bc)d", "abcd"),
    rewrite_case("(?:ab)*", "(?:ab)*"),
    rewrite_case("(?:a*)*", "(?:a*)*"),
    rewrite_case("(a)(?P<x>b)(?<y>c)", "(a)(?P<x>b)(?P<y>c)"),
    rewrite_case("a*b+c?d{2}e{2,}f{2,5}", "a*b+c?d{2}e{2,}f{2,5}"),
    rewrite_case("a{0,}b{1,}c{0,1}d{1}e{0}", "a*b+c?d{1}e{0}"),
    rewrite_case("a*?b+?c??d{2}?", "a*?b+?c??d{2}?"),
    rewrite_case("(?U)a*b*?", "a*?b*"),
    rewrite_case("(?i)ab1", "[Aa][Bb]1"),
    rewrite_case("(?i:a)b", "[Aa]b"),
    rewrite_case("a(?i)b|c", "a[Bb]|[Cc]"),
    rewrite_case("(?i)a(?-i)b", "[Aa]b"),
    rewrite_case("(?i)\u{e9}k", "[\u{c9}\u{e9}][Kk\u{212a}]"),
    rewrite_case("(?i)\u{3c3}", "[\u{3a3}\u{3c2}-\u{3c3}]"),
    rewrite_case("(?i)\u{df}1", "[\u{df}\u{1e9e}]1"),
    rewrite_case("(?i)\u{101}", "[\u{100}-\u{101}]"),
    rewrite_case("(?i)\u{4e2d}", "\u{4e2d}"),
    rewrite_case("(?u)\\bx\\B", "(?u:\\b)x(?u:\\B)"),
    rewrite_case(
      "(?u)\\s",
      "[\\x{9}-\\x{D} \u{85}\u{a0}\u{1680}\u{2000}-\u{200a}\u{2028}-\u{2029}\u{202f}\u{205f}\u{3000}]",
    ),
    rewrite_case("\\p{Zl}\\P{^Zp}", "[\u{2028}][\u{2029}]"),
    rewrite_case(
      "[\\p{Line_Separator}\\pZ]",
      "[ \u{a0}\u{1680}\u{2000}-\u{200a}\u{2028}-\u{2029}\u{202f}\u{205f}\u{3000}]",
    ),
    rewrite_case(".", "[^\\x{A}]"),
    rewrite_case("(?s).", "(?s:.)"),
    rewrite_case("^a$", "\\Aa\\z"),
    rewrite_case("(?m)^a$", "(?m:^)a(?m:$)"),
    rewrite_case("\\Aa\\z", "\\Aa\\z"),
    rewrite_case("\\bx\\B", "\\bx\\B"),
    rewrite_case("^*", "\\A*"),
    rewrite_case("[a-c]", "[a-c]"),
    rewrite_case("[^a-c]", "[^a-c]"),
    rewrite_case("[a]", "[a]"),
    rewrite_case("[]a]", "[\\]a]"),
    rewrite_case("[^]a]", "[^\\]a]"),
    rewrite_case("[a-]", "[\\-a]"),
    rewrite_case("[a-b-c]", "[\\-a-c]"),
    rewrite_case("[a\\-z]", "[\\-az]"),
    rewrite_case("[^\\x00-\\x{10FFFF}]", "[^\\x{0}-\u{10FFFF}]"),
    rewrite_case("\\d\\w\\s", "[0-9][0-9A-Z_a-z][\\x{9}-\\x{A}\\x{C}-\\x{D} ]"),
    rewrite_case("\\D", "[^0-9]"),
    rewrite_case("[\\d\\D]", "(?s:.)"),
    rewrite_case("[[:alpha:][:^digit:]]", "[^0-9]"),
    rewrite_case("[[:word:]]", "[0-9A-Z_a-z]"),
    rewrite_case("[[:alpha]", "[:\\[ahlp]"),
    rewrite_case("(?i)[k-m]", "[K-Mk-m\u{212a}]"),
    rewrite_case("(?i)[^k]", "[^Kk\u{212a}]"),
    rewrite_case("a{", "a\\{"),
    rewrite_case("a{1", "a\\{1"),
    rewrite_case("a{,2}", "a\\{,2\\}"),
    rewrite_case("a{01}", "a\\{01\\}"),
    rewrite_case("{", "\\{"),
    rewrite_case("}]", "\\}\\]"),
    rewrite_case("\\Qa.b\\E+", "a\\.b+"),
    rewrite_case("\\Qa|b", "a\\|b"),
    rewrite_case("\\Q\\Ea", "a"),
    rewrite_case("\\x41\\x{1F600}\\n\\0\\07\\011", "A\u{1F600}\\x{A}\\x{0}\\x{7}\\x{9}"),
    rewrite_case("\\a\\f\\t\\r\\v", "\\x{7}\\x{C}\\x{9}\\x{D}\\x{B}"),
    rewrite_case("\\.\\_\\-\\ ", "\\._- "),
    rewrite_case("\\x{D800}", "\\x{D800}"),
    rewrite_case("a|", "a|(?:)"),
    rewrite_case("|a", "(?:)|a"),
    rewrite_case("", "(?:)"),
    rewrite_case("()", "((?:))"),
    rewrite_case("(?:)", "(?:)"),
    rewrite_case("(?)a", "a"),
    rewrite_case("(|a)*", "((?:)|a)*"),
    rewrite_case("\u{65e5}\u{672c}+", "\u{65e5}\u{672c}+"),
  ]

test "`{c.pattern}` is rewritten as `{c.text}`, and rewriting that text again gives the same text and the same compiled program" for c: RewriteCase in rewrites {
  let re = must(c.pattern);
  let again = must(normalized_pattern(re));
  assert_eq(normalized_pattern(re), c.text);
  assert_eq(normalized_pattern(again), c.text);
  assert_eq(inner(again).instructions, inner(re).instructions);
  assert_eq(inner(again).reverse.instructions, inner(re).reverse.instructions)
}

type ErrorCase = { pattern: String, at: Int, reason: ErrorKind }

fn error_case(pattern: String, at: Int, reason: ErrorKind) -> ErrorCase =
  { pattern: pattern, at: at, reason: reason }

const error_cases: List<ErrorCase> =
  [
    error_case("(a", 0, UnclosedGroup),
    error_case("a(b(c)", 1, UnclosedGroup),
    error_case("(?i", 0, UnclosedGroup),
    error_case("(?:a", 0, UnclosedGroup),
    error_case("a)", 1, UnopenedGroup),
    error_case("(a))", 3, UnopenedGroup),
    error_case("[a", 0, UnclosedClass),
    error_case("[", 0, UnclosedClass),
    error_case("[]", 0, UnclosedClass),
    error_case("[^]", 0, UnclosedClass),
    error_case("a[b-", 1, UnclosedClass),
    error_case("[z-a]", 1, BadRange),
    error_case("[a-\\x{10}]", 1, BadRange),
    error_case("[[:nope:]]", 1, BadClassName),
    error_case("[[:^nope:]]", 1, BadClassName),
    error_case("a\\", 1, TrailingEscape),
    error_case("[a\\", 2, TrailingEscape),
    error_case("\\q", 0, BadEscape),
    error_case("\\Z", 0, BadEscape),
    error_case("\\E", 0, BadEscape),
    error_case("\\x{110000}", 0, BadEscape),
    error_case("\\x{}", 0, BadEscape),
    error_case("\\xg0", 0, BadEscape),
    error_case("\\\u{e9}", 0, BadEscape),
    error_case("[a-\\d]", 3, BadEscape),
    error_case("*a", 0, NothingToRepeat),
    error_case("a|*", 2, NothingToRepeat),
    error_case("(+)", 1, NothingToRepeat),
    error_case("{2}", 0, NothingToRepeat),
    error_case("(?i)*", 4, NothingToRepeat),
    error_case("\\Q\\E*", 4, NothingToRepeat),
    error_case("a**", 2, NestedRepeat),
    error_case("a*+", 2, NestedRepeat),
    error_case("a+?*", 3, NestedRepeat),
    error_case("a{2}{3}", 4, NestedRepeat),
    error_case("a{2,1}", 1, BadRepeat),
    error_case("a{1001}", 1, BadRepeat),
    error_case("a{2,1001}", 1, BadRepeat),
    error_case("a{99999999999999999999}", 1, BadRepeat),
    error_case("(?#note)", 2, BadGroup),
    error_case("(?>a)", 2, BadGroup),
    error_case("(?x)a", 2, BadGroup),
    error_case("(?i-)a", 4, BadGroup),
    error_case("(?i--s)a", 4, BadGroup),
    error_case("(?P>a)", 0, BadGroup),
    error_case("(?P<>a)", 4, BadGroupName),
    error_case("(?<a-b>c)", 3, BadGroupName),
    error_case("(?P<a", 4, BadGroupName),
    error_case("(?<a>x)(?P<a>y)", 11, DuplicateName),
    error_case("(a)\\1", 3, Backreference),
    error_case("\\9", 0, Backreference),
    error_case("\\141", 0, Backreference),
    error_case("\\k<a>", 0, Backreference),
    error_case("(?P<a>x)(?P=a)", 8, Backreference),
    error_case("(?=a)", 0, Lookaround),
    error_case("a(?!b)", 1, Lookaround),
    error_case("(?<=a)b", 0, Lookaround),
    error_case("(?<!a)b", 0, Lookaround),
    error_case("\\p{Klingon}", 0, UnicodeProperty),
    error_case("a\\P{greek}", 1, UnicodeProperty),
    error_case("\\pX", 0, UnicodeProperty),
    error_case("\\p", 0, UnicodeProperty),
    error_case("\\p{L", 0, UnicodeProperty),
    error_case("\\p{}", 0, UnicodeProperty),
    error_case("\\p{^}", 0, UnicodeProperty),
    error_case("\\p\u{e9}", 0, UnicodeProperty),
    error_case("[\\p{Nope}]", 1, UnicodeProperty),
    error_case("a\\C", 1, HalfCharacter),
    error_case("(a{1000}){1000}", 9, TooLarge),
    error_case("((((((((((a{10}){10}){10}){10}){10}){10}){10}){10}){10}){10})", 31, TooLarge),
  ]

test "`compile` and `read` both reject the invalid pattern `{c.pattern}`, returning the expected error reason and the position of the error" for c: ErrorCase in error_cases {
  assert_eq(compile(c.pattern), Err({ at: c.at, reason: c.reason }));
  assert_eq(try { read(c.pattern, options) }, Err({ at: c.at, reason: c.reason }))
}

fn nested(depth: Int) -> String =
  range(0, depth).fold("", |p: String, _: Int| p ++ "(") ++ "a"
    ++ range(0, depth).fold("", |p: String, _: Int| p ++ ")")

test "groups nest two hundred deep and no deeper" {
  assert_eq(group_count(must(nested(200))), 201);
  assert_eq(find(must(nested(200)), "xa"), Some({ start: 1, end: 2 }));
  assert_eq(compile(nested(201)), Err({ at: 200, reason: TooDeep }))
}

test "a pattern that compiles to more instructions than `size_limit` fails with `TooLarge`" {
  let tight = { ..options, size_limit: 8 };
  assert(match compile_with("abcdefgh", tight) { Ok(_) -> true, Err(_) -> false });
  assert_eq(compile_with("abcdefghi", tight), Err({ at: 8, reason: TooLarge }));
  assert_eq(compile_with("a{9}", tight), Err({ at: 1, reason: TooLarge }));
  assert_eq(compile_with("\u{65e5}{3}", tight), Err({ at: 1, reason: TooLarge }));
  assert_eq(compile("(a{1000}){1000}"), Err({ at: 9, reason: TooLarge }))
}

test "a byte pattern rejects characters above one byte with `NotAByte`, and matches single bytes" {
  assert_eq(compile_bytes("a\u{100}"), Err({ at: 1, reason: NotAByte }));
  assert_eq(compile_bytes("[a-\\x{100}]"), Err({ at: 3, reason: NotAByte }));
  assert_eq(compile_bytes("\\x{100}"), Err({ at: 0, reason: NotAByte }));
  assert_eq(find_bytes(must_bytes("\\xFF+"), b"a\xff\xffb"), Some({ start: 1, end: 3 }));
  assert_eq(find_bytes(must_bytes("."), b"\n\xe9"), Some({ start: 1, end: 2 }));
  assert_eq(find_bytes(must_bytes("\\C"), b"\n"), Some({ start: 0, end: 1 }));
  assert_eq(find_bytes(must_bytes("[^a]+"), b"a\x00\x80\xffa"), Some({ start: 1, end: 4 }));
  assert_eq(find_bytes(must_bytes("\u{e9}"), b"caf\xe9"), Some({ start: 3, end: 4 }));
  assert_eq(find_bytes(must_bytes("(?i)\\xE9"), b"\xc9"), None);
  assert_eq(normalized_byte_pattern(must_bytes("[^a]\\xFF")), "[^a]\\x{FF}");
  assert_eq(normalized_byte_pattern(must_bytes(".")), "[^\\x{A}]");
  assert_eq(byte_pattern(must_bytes("a|b")), "a|b")
}

fn first_slots(pattern: String, o: Options, text: String) -> List<Int> / {abort.raise} = {
  let c = inner(must_with(pattern, o));
  match matches(c, Bytes::of_string(text), 2 * c.names.len(), 1) {
    [slots] -> slots.to_list(),
    _ -> [],
  }
}

type Sample = { pattern: String, text: String, slots: List<Int> }

fn sample(pattern: String, text: String, slots: List<Int>) -> Sample =
  { pattern: pattern, text: text, slots: slots }

const samples: List<Sample> =
  [
    sample("a+", "baaac", [1, 4]),
    sample("a*", "baaac", [0, 0]),
    sample("(a+)(b+)", "xaabbby", [1, 6, 1, 3, 3, 6]),
    sample("a|ab", "xab", [1, 2]),
    sample("ab|a", "xab", [1, 3]),
    sample("(a*)*", "b", [0, 0, 0, 0]),
    sample("(a*)+", "b", [0, 0, 0, 0]),
    sample("(a|b)*c", "abcabc", [0, 3, 1, 2]),
    sample("^abc$", "abc", [0, 3]),
    sample("^abc$", "abcd", []),
    sample("abc$", "abc\n", []),
    sample("\\bfoo\\b", "a foo b", [2, 5]),
    sample("\\bfoo\\b", "afoo b", []),
    sample("(?m)^b$", "a\nb\nc", [2, 3]),
    sample("x*", "\u{e9}", [0, 0]),
    sample(".", "\u{e9}x", [0, 2]),
    sample("[^a]", "a\u{1F600}", [1, 5]),
    sample("[\u{3b1}-\u{3c9}]+", "abc \u{3b1}\u{3b2}\u{3b3} d", [4, 10]),
    sample("\u{e9}", "cafe\u{301} caf\u{e9}", [10, 12]),
    sample("\\B", "a\u{e9}", [3, 3]),
    sample("\\x{D800}|b", "ab", [1, 2]),
    sample("a.c", "a\nc abc", [4, 7]),
    sample("(?s)a.c", "a\nc abc", [0, 3]),
    sample("a{2,3}", "aaaa", [0, 3]),
    sample("a{2,3}?", "aaaa", [0, 2]),
    sample("(?U)a{2,3}", "aaaa", [0, 2]),
    sample("(a)|(b)", "b", [0, 1, -1, -1, 0, 1]),
    sample("(a){0}b", "ab", [1, 2, -1, -1]),
    sample("(?i)straSSe", "STRASSE", [0, 7]),
    sample("(?i)k", "\u{212a}K", [0, 3]),
    sample("(?i)\u{3c3}+", "o\u{3a3}\u{3c2}\u{3c3}s", [1, 7]),
    sample("(?i)stra\u{df}e", "STRA\u{1e9e}E", [0, 8]),
    sample("\\p{Greek}+", "ab\u{3b1}\u{3b2}c", [2, 6]),
    sample("\\P{Greek}+", "\u{3b1}bc\u{3b2}", [2, 4]),
    sample("\\p{^Greek}", "\u{3b1}b", [2, 3]),
    sample("\\P{^Greek}", "b\u{3b1}", [1, 3]),
    sample("\\pL\\p{Nd}", "-\u{e9}\u{663}", [1, 5]),
    sample("[\\p{Lu}\\d]+", "a\u{c9}7Bc", [1, 5]),
    sample("(?i)\\p{Lu}+", "a\u{e9}1", [0, 3]),
    sample("\\p{Any}", "\u{1f600}", [0, 4]),
    sample("\\w+", "na\u{ef}ve", [0, 2]),
    sample("(?u)\\w+", "na\u{ef}ve", [0, 6]),
    sample("(?u)\\d+", "x\u{663}\u{664}y", [1, 5]),
    sample("\\d+", "x\u{663}4y", [3, 4]),
    sample("(?u)\\s", "a\u{3000}b", [1, 4]),
    sample("(?u)\\W", "\u{e9}-", [2, 3]),
    sample("\\b\\w+\\b", "\u{e9}t\u{e9} ok", [2, 3]),
    sample("(?u)\\b\\w+\\b", "\u{e9}t\u{e9} ok", [0, 5]),
    sample("(?u)\\b", "\u{e9}", [0, 0]),
    sample("(?u)\\B", "\u{e9}", []),
    sample("(?u)a\\B.", "a\u{e9}", [0, 3]),
    sample("(?u)a\\b.", "a\u{e9}", []),
    sample("a\\b.", "a\u{e9}", [0, 3]),
    sample("(?u:\\w)\\w", "\u{e9}a\u{e9}", [0, 3]),
    sample("foo|bar|baz", "xx baz", [3, 6]),
    sample("", "abc", [0, 0]),
    sample("$", "abc", [3, 3]),
    sample("\\d+-\\d+", "tel 555-1234 ok", [4, 12]),
    sample("[[:upper:]][[:lower:]]+", "say Hello", [4, 9]),
    sample("needle", "a haystack with a needle in it, and a second needle", [18, 24]),
    sample("(\\w+)@(\\w+)\\.com", "write to someone@example.com today", [9, 28, 9, 16, 17, 24]),
    sample("[0-9]+$", "one 1 two 22 three 333", [19, 22]),
    sample("(?:x|y)*z", "the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog", [37, 38]),
    sample("[a-z]+ing\\b", "the quick brown fox was jumping over the lazy dog", [24, 31]),
    sample("[a-z]+ing\\b", "the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog, singly", []),
    sample("(\\w+)@example\\.com", "from a@example.org and bee@example.com, both", [
      23,
      38,
      23,
      26,
    ]),
  ]

test "`{c.pattern}` matched against `{c.text}` with the matcher that tracks all possible positions in the pattern at once finds the expected match positions" for c: Sample in samples {
  assert_eq(first_slots(c.pattern, threads_only, c.text), c.slots)
}

test "`{c.pattern}` matched against `{c.text}` with the matcher that tries one path through the pattern at a time finds the expected match positions" for c: Sample in samples {
  assert_eq(first_slots(c.pattern, states_always, c.text), c.slots)
}

test "`{c.pattern}` matched against `{c.text}` with the one-path matcher limited to three saved positions finds the expected match positions" for c: Sample in samples {
  assert_eq(first_slots(c.pattern, states_cramped, c.text), c.slots)
}

test "with the `longest` option, the leftmost match is the longest one, and without it the first alternative that matches wins" {
  let longest = { ..options, longest: true };
  assert_eq(first_slots("a|ab|abc", options, "xabcd"), [1, 2]);
  assert_eq(first_slots("a|ab|abc", longest, "xabcd"), [1, 4]);
  assert_eq(first_slots("a|ab|abc", { ..longest, short: -1 }, "xabcd"), [1, 4]);
  assert_eq(first_slots("a|ab|abc", { ..longest, short: -1, state_limit: 3 }, "xabcd"), [1, 4]);
  assert_eq(first_slots("(a*?)(a*)", longest, "aaa"), [0, 3, 0, 0, 0, 3]);
  assert_eq(first_slots("a*?", longest, "aaa"), [0, 3])
}

fn spans(pairs: List<Int>) -> List<Span> =
  range(0, pairs.len() / 2).fold([], |accumulator: List<Span>, i: Int|
    accumulator.push({ start: pairs.at_or(2 * i, 0), end: pairs.at_or(2 * i + 1, 0) }))

test "`find_all` returns matches in order without overlap, and never returns an empty match at the position where the previous match ended" {
  assert_eq(find_all(must("a"), "bababaab"), spans([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 6, 7]));
  assert_eq(find_all(must("a*"), "baaab"), spans([0, 0, 1, 4, 5, 5]));
  assert_eq(find_all(must(""), "ab"), spans([0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2]));
  assert_eq(find_all(must(""), "\u{e9}\u{1F600}"), spans([0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2]));
  assert_eq(find_all(must("\\b"), "x y"), spans([0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3]));
  assert_eq(find_all(must("x"), ""), []);
  assert_eq(find_all(must("^a"), "aaa"), spans([0, 1]));
  assert_eq(find_all(must("(?m)^."), "ab\ncd"), spans([0, 1, 3, 4]));
  assert_eq(find_all(must("\u{e9}+"), "\u{e9}t\u{e9}\u{e9}"), spans([0, 1, 2, 4]));
  assert_eq(find_all_bytes(must_bytes("a*"), b"baaab"), spans([0, 0, 1, 4, 5, 5]));
  assert_eq(find_all_bytes(must_bytes(""), b"\xc3\xa9"), spans([0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2]))
}

test "a match's groups are read by number and by name, in characters of the text" {
  let re = must("(?P<year>\\d{4})-(?P<month>\\d{2})(-(?P<day>\\d{2}))?");
  assert_eq(group_count(re), 5);
  assert_eq(group_names(re), [None, Some("year"), Some("month"), None, Some("day")]);
  let text = "\u{e9}t\u{e9} 2026-10, puis 2027-01-15";
  let first = match captures(re, text) { Some(c) -> c, None -> panic("a date is there") };
  assert_eq(group(first, 0), Some({ start: 4, end: 11 }));
  assert_eq(named(first, "year"), Some({ start: 4, end: 8 }));
  assert_eq(named(first, "month"), Some({ start: 9, end: 11 }));
  assert_eq(named(first, "day"), None);
  assert_eq(named(first, "hour"), None);
  assert_eq(group(first, 5), None);
  assert_eq(group(first, -1), None);
  assert_eq(match named(first, "year") { Some(s) -> slice(text, s), None -> "" }, "2026");
  let all = captures_all(re, text);
  assert_eq(all.map(|c: Captures| named(c, "day")), [None, Some({ start: 26, end: 28 })]);
  assert_eq(captures(re, "no date"), None);
  let bytes = must_bytes("(a)(?P<rest>[\\x80-\\xFF]*)");
  assert_eq(
    match captures_bytes(bytes, b"xa\xff\xfe") { Some(c) -> named(c, "rest"), None -> None },
    Some({ start: 2, end: 4 }),
  );
  assert_eq(captures_all_bytes(bytes, b"a a\x80").len(), 2)
}

test "a template inserts groups by number and by name, and fails for a group the pattern does not have" {
  let re = must("(?P<first>\\w+) (?P<last>\\w+)");
  assert_eq(
    replace(re, "ada lovelace, alan turing", must_template(re, "$last, $first")),
    "lovelace, ada, alan turing",
  );
  assert_eq(
    replace_all(re, "ada lovelace, alan turing", must_template(re, "${2}_$1")),
    "lovelace_ada, turing_alan",
  );
  assert_eq(
    replace_all(re, "ada lovelace", must_template(re, "<$0> costs $$5")),
    "<ada lovelace> costs $5",
  );
  assert_eq(replace_all(re, "ada lovelace", must_template(re, "${first}s")), "adas");
  assert_eq(replace_all(must("a(x)?"), "a ax", must_template(must("a(x)?"), "[$1]")), "[] [x]");
  assert_eq(
    replace_all(must("\u{e9}"), "\u{e9}t\u{e9}", must_template(must("\u{e9}"), "e")),
    "ete",
  );
  assert_eq(replace_all(must("x*"), "abc", must_template(must("x*"), "-")), "-a-b-c-");
  assert_eq(template(re, "$3"), Err({ at: 0, reason: NoSuchGroup }));
  assert_eq(template(re, "a $middle"), Err({ at: 2, reason: NoSuchGroup }));
  assert_eq(template(re, "$1st"), Err({ at: 0, reason: NoSuchGroup }));
  assert_eq(template(re, "${}"), Err({ at: 0, reason: NoSuchGroup }));
  assert_eq(template(re, "${first"), Err({ at: 0, reason: UnclosedName }));
  assert_eq(template(re, "cost: $"), Err({ at: 6, reason: LoneDollar }));
  assert_eq(template(re, "$ 1"), Err({ at: 0, reason: LoneDollar }));
  let bytes = must_bytes("(\\x00+)");
  let is_unicode = match template_bytes(bytes, "<$1>") {
    Ok(t) -> t,
    Err(_) -> panic("a template"),
  };
  assert_eq(replace_all_bytes(bytes, b"a\x00\x00b\x00", is_unicode), b"a<\x00\x00>b<\x00>");
  assert_eq(replace_bytes(bytes, b"a\x00\x00b\x00", is_unicode), b"a<\x00\x00>b\x00")
}

test "a match is replaced by what a function returns for what it captured" {
  let re = must("(\\d+)([a-z]?)");
  let text = "1a 22 333c";
  let doubled = replace_all_with(re, text, |c: Captures|
    match group(c, 1) { Some(s) -> slice(text, s) ++ slice(text, s), None -> "" });
  assert_eq(doubled, "11 2222 333333");
  assert_eq(replace_with(re, text, |_: Captures| ""), " 22 333c");
  assert_eq(replace_all_with(must("z"), text, |_: Captures| "!"), text)
}

test "`split` cuts a string at each match and returns one more piece than there are matches" {
  assert_eq(split(must(","), "a,b,,c"), ["a", "b", "", "c"]);
  assert_eq(split(must(",\\s*"), "a, b,c,   d"), ["a", "b", "c", "d"]);
  assert_eq(split(must(","), ""), [""]);
  assert_eq(split(must(","), ","), ["", ""]);
  assert_eq(split(must("x*"), "abc"), ["", "a", "b", "c", ""]);
  assert_eq(split(must(""), "\u{e9}a"), ["", "\u{e9}", "a", ""]);
  assert_eq(splitn(must(","), "a,b,,c", 2), ["a", "b,,c"]);
  assert_eq(splitn(must(","), "a,b,,c", 1), ["a,b,,c"]);
  assert_eq(splitn(must(","), "a,b,,c", 9), ["a", "b", "", "c"]);
  assert_eq(splitn(must(","), "a,b,,c", 0), []);
  assert_eq(split_bytes(must_bytes("\\x00"), b"a\x00b\x00"), [b"a", b"b", b""]);
  assert_eq(splitn_bytes(must_bytes("\\x00"), b"a\x00b\x00", 2), [b"a", b"b\x00"])
}

test "`escape` returns a pattern that matches exactly the given text and nothing else" {
  assert_eq(escape("a.b*c"), "a\\.b\\*c");
  assert_eq(escape("\\.+*?()|[]{}^$"), "\\\\\\.\\+\\*\\?\\(\\)\\|\\[\\]\\{\\}\\^\\$");
  assert_eq(escape("plain \u{e9} text"), "plain \u{e9} text");
  assert_eq(find(must(escape("1+1=2?")), "is 1+1=2? yes"), Some({ start: 3, end: 9 }))
}

test "two patterns are equal when their text and options are equal, and a pattern formats as its source text" {
  assert(must("a+") == must("a+"));
  assert(must("a+") != must("a+?"));
  assert(must("a+") != must_with("a+", { ..options, longest: true }));
  assert_eq(f"{must("(?i)a|b")}", "(?i)a|b");
  assert_eq(pattern(must("(?i)a|b")), "(?i)a|b")
}

test "a search skips to where a match can start, and a pattern that is plain text is searched as text" {
  let anywhere = inner(must("[0-9]+x"));
  assert_eq(anywhere.prefilter.first, b"0123456789");
  assert_eq(anywhere.prefilter.prefix, b"");
  let led = inner(must("abc[0-9]"));
  assert_eq(led.prefilter.prefix, b"abc");
  assert(!led.prefilter.exact);
  let exact = inner(must("a\\.b"));
  assert_eq(exact.prefilter.prefix, b"a.b");
  assert(exact.prefilter.exact);
  assert_eq(inner(must("a*b")).prefilter.first, b"ab");
  assert_eq(inner(must("a*")).prefilter.first, b"");
  assert_eq(inner(must("\\ba")).prefilter.first, b"");
  assert_eq(inner(must("(?i)k")).prefilter.first, b"Kk\xe2");
  assert_eq(inner(must("(?i)x")).prefilter.first, b"Xx");
  assert_eq(inner(must(".")).prefilter.first.len(), 178);
  assert_eq(inner(must("\\w+@example\\.com")).prefilter.required, b"@example.com");
  assert_eq(inner(must("(\\d+)(?:ab)+\u{e9}|x")).prefilter.required, b"");
  assert_eq(inner(must("\\d(?:ab)+c\u{e9}\\d")).prefilter.required, b"c\xc3\xa9");
  assert_eq(inner(must("\\d(?:ab){0,2}(c)\\d")).prefilter.required, b"c");
  assert_eq(inner(must("(?i)abc\\d")).prefilter.required, b"");
  assert_eq(inner(must("abc\\d")).prefilter.required, b"");
  assert_eq(byte_inner(must_bytes("\\d\\xFF\\x00")).prefilter.required, b"\xff\x00");
  let mail = must("\\w+@example\\.com");
  let absent = run_of_a(100000);
  assert_eq(find(mail, absent), None);
  assert_eq(find(mail, absent ++ "@example.com"), Some({ start: 0, end: 100012 }));
  assert(!is_match(mail, absent));
  assert_eq(find_all(mail, "a@example.com b@example.org c@example.com").len(), 2);
  assert_eq(byte_inner(must_bytes("(?s).a")).prefilter.first, b"")
}

fn run_of_a(n: Int) -> String / {abort.raise} = String::of_bytes(run_of(97, n))

const pathological: List<String> =
  [
    "(a*)*b",
    "(a|aa)*b",
    "(a+)+b",
    "(.*)*x",
    "(a*)*(a*)*(a*)*b",
    "(?:a?){30}a{30}b",
    "(a|a|a|a|a|a|a|a)*b",
  ]

test "`{pattern}` finds no match in 4000 a's with either matcher or with `is_match`, without blowing up in time" for pattern: String in pathological {
  let text = run_of_a(4000);
  let found = |o: Options|
    has_match_by_states(inner(must_with(pattern, o)), Bytes::of_string(text));
  assert(!found(threads_only));
  assert(!found(options));
  assert(!is_match(must(pattern), text))
}

test "the required text of `(a*)*b` is `b`, because every match of that pattern contains a `b`" {
  assert_eq(inner(must("(a*)*b")).prefilter.required, b"b")
}

fn generated_cases() -> gen::Gen<GeneratedCase> =
  gen::map2(
    gen::list(gen::any_int()),
    gen::list(gen::any_int()),
    |pattern: List<Int>, text: List<Int>| { pattern: pattern, text: text },
  )

fn tricky(seeds: List<Int>) -> String =
  String::join(
    seeds.map(|n: Int|
      [
        "\\",
        ".",
        "+",
        "*",
        "?",
        "(",
        ")",
        "|",
        "[",
        "]",
        "{",
        "}",
        "^",
        "$",
        "-",
        ",",
        "a",
        "b",
        "E",
        "Q",
        "d",
        "1",
        " ",
        "\n",
        "\u{e9}",
        "\u{1F600}",
        ":",
        "<",
        ">",
        "=",
        "!",
        "#",
      ].at_or(
        n & 31,
        "a",
      )),
    "",
  )

test "under `(?u)`, `\\b` matches exactly where one neighboring character is a `\\w` character and the other is not" {
  let wordy = must("(?u)^\\w$");
  let edge = must("(?u)\\b");
  gen::check(
    gen::any_int(),
    |seed: Int| {
      let text = char::sample_text(seed);
      let chars = Array::of_list(text.chars());
      let is_wordy = |i: Int|
        match chars.at(i) { Some(c) -> is_match(wordy, String::of_chars([c])), None -> false };
      find_all(edge, text).map(|s: Span| s.start)
        == range(0, chars.len() + 1).filter(|i: Int| is_wordy(i - 1) != is_wordy(i))
    },
    cases: 8,
  )
}

test "Unicode property patterns find the same matches with every matcher setting, including the one-path matcher limited to three saved positions" {
  let text = String::join(
    range(0, 60).map(|_: Int| "na\u{ef}ve \u{391}\u{3b2}\u{3b3}\u{663}7 \u{4e2d}\u{6587}_x9\n"),
    "",
  );
  let found = |pattern: String, o: Options| find_all(must_with(pattern, o), text);
  [
    "\\p{L}+",
    "(?i)\\p{Lu}\\p{Greek}*",
    "[\\p{L}\\p{Nd}_]+ ",
    "(?u)\\w+\\s\\d?",
    "\\P{L}+",
    "(?u)\\b\\w",
    "\\p{Han}{2}",
    "(?i)\\x{3a3}?\\x{3b1}",
  ].fold((), |_: Unit, pattern: String| {
    let by_threads = found(pattern, threads_only);
    assert(by_threads.len() >= 60, Some(pattern));
    assert_eq(found(pattern, states_always), by_threads);
    assert_eq(found(pattern, states_cramped), by_threads);
    assert_eq(found(pattern, options), by_threads)
  })
}

test "a Unicode property class compiles to a program under the size limit, and a pattern that exceeds the limit fails with `TooLarge`" {
  let size = |pattern: String| inner(must(pattern)).instructions.len();
  let rejected = |pattern: String, o: Options|
    match compile_with(pattern, o) { Err(error_case) -> Some(error_case), Ok(_) -> None };
  assert(size("\\p{L}") > 300 && size("\\p{L}") < 4000, Some(size("\\p{L}").to_string()));
  assert(size("(?u)\\w") < 4000, Some(size("(?u)\\w").to_string()));
  assert(size("\\p{Greek}") < 200, Some(size("\\p{Greek}").to_string()));
  assert(size("\\p{L}{20}") < options.size_limit);
  assert_eq(rejected("\\p{L}", { ..options, size_limit: 100 }), Some({ at: 0, reason: TooLarge }));
  assert_eq(rejected("\\p{L}{1000}", options), Some({ at: 5, reason: TooLarge }));
  assert_eq(rejected("\\p{L}{1000}", { ..options, size_limit: 10000000 }), None)
}

test "a byte pattern rejects Unicode properties and `(?u)`, and its case-insensitive matching covers only ASCII letters" {
  let rejected = |pattern: String|
    match compile_bytes(pattern) { Err(error_case) -> Some(error_case), Ok(_) -> None };
  assert_eq(rejected("\\pL"), Some({ at: 0, reason: UnicodeProperty }));
  assert_eq(rejected("[\\p{Greek}]"), Some({ at: 1, reason: UnicodeProperty }));
  assert_eq(rejected("(?u)\\w"), Some({ at: 2, reason: BadGroup }));
  assert_eq(find_bytes(must_bytes("(?i)k"), b"\xe2\x84\xaaK"), Some({ start: 3, end: 4 }));
  assert_eq(find(must("(?i)k"), "\u{212a}K"), Some({ start: 0, end: 1 }))
}

test "an escaped text compiles, and matches that text and no other" {
  gen::check(
    gen::map2(
      gen::list(gen::any_int()),
      gen::list(gen::any_int()),
      |text: List<Int>, other: List<Int>| { text: text, other: other },
    ),
    |x: { text: List<Int>, other: List<Int> }|
      agrees(
        |d: { text: List<Int>, other: List<Int> }| {
          let text = tricky(d.text);
          let other = tricky(d.other);
          let whole = must("\\A(?:" ++ escape(text) ++ ")\\z");
          is_match(whole, text) && is_match(whole, other) == (other == text)
            && find(must(escape(text)), text) == Some({ start: 0, end: text.len() })
        },
        |_: { text: List<Int>, other: List<Int> }| true,
        x,
      ),
  )
}

type GeneratedCase = { pattern: List<Int>, text: List<Int> }

fn pattern_from(seeds: List<Int>, looks: Bool) -> String =
  String::join(
    seeds.take(10).fold([], |stack: List<String>, n: Int|
      grow_pattern(stack, n & 15, n >> 4 & 3, looks)),
    "",
  )

fn grow_pattern(stack: List<String>, step: Int, pick: Int, looks: Bool) -> List<String> = {
  let last = stack.at_or(stack.len() - 1, "a");
  let before = stack.at_or(stack.len() - 2, "b");
  match step {
    0 | 1 | 2 -> stack.push(["a", "b", "c", "ab"].at_or(pick, "a")),
    3 -> stack.push([".", "[ab]", "[^a]", "\\w"].at_or(pick, ".")),
    4 -> stack.push(if looks { ["^", "$", "\\b", "\\B"].at_or(pick, "^") } else { "" }),
    5 | 6 -> stack.take(stack.len() - 2).push(before ++ last),
    7 | 8 -> stack.take(stack.len() - 2).push("(?:" ++ before ++ "|" ++ last ++ ")"),
    9 | 10 ->
      stack.take(stack.len() - 1).push(
        "(?:" ++ last ++ ")" ++ ["*", "+", "?", "{1,2}"].at_or(pick, "*"),
      ),
    11 ->
      stack.take(stack.len() - 1).push(
        "(?:" ++ last ++ ")" ++ ["*?", "+?", "??", "{2}"].at_or(pick, "*?"),
      ),
    12 | 13 -> stack.take(stack.len() - 1).push("(" ++ last ++ ")"),
    _ -> stack.push(if looks { "(?m:^)" } else { "a" }),
  }
}

fn text_from(seeds: List<Int>) -> String =
  String::join(
    seeds.take(10).map(|n: Int| ["a", "a", "a", "b", "b", "c", " ", "\n"].at_or(n & 7, "a")),
    "",
  )

fn all_slots(pattern: String, o: Options, text: String) -> List<List<Int>> / {abort.raise} = {
  let c = inner(must_with(pattern, o));
  matches(c, Bytes::of_string(text), 2 * c.names.len(), -1).map(|slots: Array<Int>| slots.to_list())
}

test "on generated patterns and texts, the one-path matcher finds the same matches as the matcher that tracks all positions at once" {
  gen::check(generated_cases(), |x: GeneratedCase|
    agrees(
      |d: GeneratedCase| all_slots(pattern_from(d.pattern, true), states_always, text_from(d.text)),
      |d: GeneratedCase| all_slots(pattern_from(d.pattern, true), threads_only, text_from(d.text)),
      x,
    ))
}

fn backtracking_match(
  node: Node,
  hay: Bytes,
  at: Int,
  fuel: Int,
  then: (Int) -> Bool / {abort.raise},
) -> Bool / {abort.raise} =
  if fuel <= 0 { panic("a pattern is nested more deeply than the matcher allows") } else {
    match node {
      Empty -> then(at),
      Literal(c) -> at < hay.len() && hay.at(at) == c && then(at + 1),
      Class(set) ->
        at < hay.len()
          && set.fold(false, |checked_size: Bool, i: Interval|
            checked_size || (hay.at(at) >= i.lo && hay.at(at) <= i.hi))
          && then(at + 1),
      Looking(look) -> look_bits(look, false) & ~looks_at(hay, at, true) == 0 && then(at),
      Concat(items) -> backtracking_sequence(items, 0, hay, at, fuel - 1, then),
      Alternate(items) ->
        items.fold(false, |any: Bool, n: Node|
          any || backtracking_match(n, hay, at, fuel - 1, then)),
      Repeat(sub, least, most, _) -> backtracking_repeat(sub, least, most, hay, at, fuel - 1, then),
      Capture(_, _, sub) -> backtracking_match(sub, hay, at, fuel - 1, then),
    }
  }

fn backtracking_sequence(
  items: List<Node>,
  i: Int,
  hay: Bytes,
  at: Int,
  fuel: Int,
  then: (Int) -> Bool / {abort.raise},
) -> Bool / {abort.raise} =
  if fuel <= 0 { panic("a pattern is nested more deeply than the matcher allows") } else {
    match items.at(i) {
      None -> then(at),
      Some(n) ->
        backtracking_match(n, hay, at, fuel - 1, |next: Int|
          backtracking_sequence(items, i + 1, hay, next, fuel - 1, then)),
    }
  }

fn backtracking_repeat(
  sub: Node,
  least: Int,
  most: Int,
  hay: Bytes,
  at: Int,
  fuel: Int,
  then: (Int) -> Bool / {abort.raise},
) -> Bool / {abort.raise} =
  if fuel <= 0 { panic("a pattern is nested more deeply than the matcher allows") }
  else if least > 0 {
    backtracking_match(sub, hay, at, fuel - 1, |next: Int|
      backtracking_repeat(
        sub,
        least - 1,
        if most < 0 { most } else { most - 1 },
        hay,
        next,
        fuel - 1,
        then,
      ))
  } else {
    then(at)
      || (most != 0
      && backtracking_match(sub, hay, at, fuel - 1, |next: Int|
        next > at
          && backtracking_repeat(
            sub,
            0,
            if most < 0 { most } else { most - 1 },
            hay,
            next,
            fuel - 1,
            then,
          )))
  }

test "a pattern matches a whole text exactly when a backtracking match over the pattern's parsed tree also matches it" {
  gen::check(generated_cases(), |x: GeneratedCase|
    agrees(
      |d: GeneratedCase|
        is_match(must("\\A(?:" ++ pattern_from(d.pattern, true) ++ ")\\z"), text_from(d.text)),
      |d: GeneratedCase| {
        let hay = Bytes::of_string(text_from(d.text));
        backtracking_match(
          inner(must(pattern_from(d.pattern, true))).tree,
          hay,
          0,
          2000,
          |end: Int| end == hay.len(),
        )
      },
      x,
    ))
}

test "`find_all` returns matches in order without overlap, and each match alone matches the whole pattern" {
  gen::check(generated_cases(), |x: GeneratedCase|
    agrees(
      |d: GeneratedCase| {
        let text = text_from(d.text);
        let whole = must("\\A(?:" ++ pattern_from(d.pattern, false) ++ ")\\z");
        find_all(must(pattern_from(d.pattern, false)), text).fold(
          { ok: true, at: 0 },
          |rewrite_case: { ok: Bool, at: Int }, s: Span|
            {
              ok: rewrite_case.ok && s.start >= rewrite_case.at && s.end >= s.start
                && is_match(whole, slice(text, s)),
              at: s.end,
            },
        ).ok
      },
      |_: GeneratedCase| true,
      x,
    ))
}

test "joining the pieces from `split` with the matches between them gives back the original text" {
  gen::check(generated_cases(), |x: GeneratedCase|
    agrees(
      |d: GeneratedCase| {
        let text = text_from(d.text);
        let re = must(pattern_from(d.pattern, true));
        let between = find_all(re, text).map(|s: Span| slice(text, s));
        enumerate(split(re, text)).fold(
          "",
          |accumulator: String, part: { index: Int, value: String }|
            accumulator ++ part.value ++ between.at_or(part.index, ""),
        )
      },
      |d: GeneratedCase| text_from(d.text),
      x,
    ))
}

test "a pattern rewritten by `normalized_pattern` compiles to the same program as the original pattern" {
  gen::check(generated_cases(), |x: GeneratedCase|
    agrees(
      |d: GeneratedCase| {
        let again = inner(must(normalized_pattern(must(pattern_from(d.pattern, true)))));
        {
          ahead: again.instructions,
          back: again.reverse.instructions,
          classes: again.finder.classes,
        }
      },
      |d: GeneratedCase| {
        let first = inner(must(pattern_from(d.pattern, true)));
        {
          ahead: first.instructions,
          back: first.reverse.instructions,
          classes: first.finder.classes,
        }
      },
      x,
    ))
}
